{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523734474,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f31d13001b4rbH7Nfd689DP","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f31377001QY1KNqFZrT0zCj","type":"tool","id":"call_25632fccc79e4655a0265804","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":758,"limit":140},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 758-897\n758:       step_graph_convergence:\n759:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n760:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n761:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n762:         outputs:\n763:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n764:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n765:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n766:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n767:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n768:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n769:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n770: \n771:       step_check_convergence:\n772:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n773:         algorithm: |\n774:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n775:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n776:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n777:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: steps 4 and 5 are telemetry only and cannot set STOP or BLOCKED. Record weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\" and choose a broader next focus.\n778:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n779:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n780:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n781:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n782:                signals = []\n783:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n784:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n785:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n786:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n787:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n788:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n789:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n790:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n791:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n792:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n793:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n794:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n795:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n796:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n797:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n798:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n799:                  stop_blocked = true\n800:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n801:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n802:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n803:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n804:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n805:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n806:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n807:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n808:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n809:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n810:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n811:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n812:                  stop_blocked = false\n813:           6. else: CONTINUE\n814:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n815:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n816:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n817:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n818:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n819:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n820:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n821:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n822:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n823:                if not guardResult.passed:\n824:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n825:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n826:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n827:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n828:         outputs:\n829:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n830:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n831:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n832:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n833:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n834:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n835:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n836:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n837:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n838:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n839:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n840:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n841:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n842:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n843: \n844:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n845:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n846:         if_pass:\n847:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n848:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n849: \n850:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n851:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n852:         if_blocked:\n853:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n854:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n855:           set:\n856:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n857:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n858:             stop_blocked: false\n859: \n860:       step_handle_convergence:\n861:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n862:         if_stop:\n863:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n864:           if_divergent_eligible:\n865:             eligibility_contract:\n866:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n867:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n868:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n869:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n870:             steps:\n871:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n872:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n873:                 command: |\n874:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n875:                   import {\n876:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n877:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n878:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n879:                   import {\n880:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n881:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n882: \n883:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n884:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n885:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n886:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n887:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n888:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n889:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n890:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n891:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n892:                   });\n893:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n894:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n895:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n896:                         seat.id,\n897:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 898]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 758-897\n758:       step_graph_convergence:\n759:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n760:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n761:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n762:         outputs:\n763:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n764:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n765:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n766:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n767:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n768:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n769:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n770: \n771:       step_check_convergence:\n772:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n773:         algorithm: |\n774:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n775:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n776:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n777:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: steps 4 and 5 are telemetry only and cannot set STOP or BLOCKED. Record weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\" and choose a broader next focus.\n778:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n779:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n780:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n781:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n782:                signals = []\n783:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n784:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n785:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n786:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n787:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n788:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n789:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n790:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n791:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n792:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n793:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n794:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n795:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n796:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n797:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n798:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n799:                  stop_blocked = true\n800:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n801:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n802:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n803:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n804:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n805:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n806:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n807:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n808:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n809:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n810:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n811:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n812:                  stop_blocked = false\n813:           6. else: CONTINUE\n814:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n815:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n816:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n817:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n818:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n819:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n820:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n821:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n822:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n823:                if not guardResult.passed:\n824:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n825:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n826:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n827:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n828:         outputs:\n829:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n830:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n831:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n832:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n833:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n834:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n835:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n836:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n837:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n838:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n839:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n840:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n841:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n842:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n843: \n844:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n845:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n846:         if_pass:\n847:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n848:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n849: \n850:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n851:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n852:         if_blocked:\n853:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n854:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n855:           set:\n856:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n857:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n858:             stop_blocked: false\n859: \n860:       step_handle_convergence:\n861:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n862:         if_stop:\n863:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n864:           if_divergent_eligible:\n865:             eligibility_contract:\n866:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n867:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n868:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n869:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n870:             steps:\n871:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n872:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n873:                 command: |\n874:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n875:                   import {\n876:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n877:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n878:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n879:                   import {\n880:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n881:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n882: \n883:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n884:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n885:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n886:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n887:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n888:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n889:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n890:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n891:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n892:                   });\n893:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n894:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n895:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n896:                         seat.id,\n897:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 898]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\",\"offset\":758,\"limit\":140}"},"time":{"start":1794523733267,"end":1794523734474}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523734478,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f31e9a001WG8JAPZJZPpL3Y","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f31377001QY1KNqFZrT0zCj","type":"tool","id":"call_c0b9da36f92e435d9bcd4d94","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":1930,"limit":80},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 1930-2009\n1930:           message: \"The {unavailable_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({unavailable_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1931:           halt: true\n1932:         if_absent:\n1933:           action: \"Continue to state reduction\"\n1934: \n1935:       step_reduce_state:\n1936:         action: \"Run the reducer to synchronize registry, dashboard, and strategy\"\n1937:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n1938:         inputs:\n1939:           latestJSONLDelta: \"Latest JSONL records written since the previous iteration\"\n1940:           newIterationFile: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1941:           priorReducedState: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1942:         outputs:\n1943:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1944:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1945:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1946:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} question_conflict events when inbox text disagrees with registry-owned question text\"\n1947:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} idempotent idea_promoted events when observed ideas reach minIdeaObservations\"\n1948:           - \"{state_paths.registry} observedIdeas, promotedIdeas, suppressedIdeas, rejectedPatterns, and suppressedCandidates from idea lifecycle events\"\n1949:         failure_modes:\n1950:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1951:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1952:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1953:           question_conflict: \"keep registry value + append question_conflict event with inboxValue, registryValue, and operatorDecision\"\n1954:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n1955: \n1956:       step_graph_upsert:\n1957:         action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n1958:         note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n1959:         command: |\n1960:           node <<'EOF'\n1961:           const { existsSync, readFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n1962:           const { join } = require('node:path');\n1963:           const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n1964: \n1965:           const deltaDir = '{state_paths.delta_dir}';\n1966:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n1967:           const iteration = Number('{current_iteration}');\n1968:           const specFolder = '{spec_folder}';\n1969:           const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n1970: \n1971:           function parseJsonLines(raw, source) {\n1972:             const records = [];\n1973:             for (const line of raw.split(/\\r?\\n/)) {\n1974:               const trimmed = line.trim();\n1975:               if (!trimmed) continue;\n1976:               try {\n1977:                 records.push(JSON.parse(trimmed));\n1978:               } catch (error) {\n1979:                 process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: skipped malformed line in ${source}: ${error.message}\\n`);\n1980:               }\n1981:             }\n1982:             return records;\n1983:           }\n1984: \n1985:           function latestGraphEvents(records) {\n1986:             for (let index = records.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n1987:               const record = records[index];\n1988:               if (record && record.type === 'iteration') {\n1989:                 return Array.isArray(record.graphEvents) ? record.graphEvents : [];\n1990:               }\n1991:             }\n1992:             return [];\n1993:           }\n1994: \n1995:           const deltaPath = join(deltaDir, `iter-${String(iteration).padStart(3, '0')}.jsonl`);\n1996:           const sourcePath = existsSync(deltaPath) ? deltaPath : stateLogPath;\n1997:           const records = existsSync(sourcePath) ? parseJsonLines(readFileSync(sourcePath, 'utf8'), sourcePath) : [];\n1998:           const events = latestGraphEvents(records);\n1999: \n2000:           const nodes = [];\n2001:           const edges = [];\n2002:           for (const event of events) {\n2003:             if (!event || typeof event !== 'object') continue;\n2004:             if (event.type === 'node') {\n2005:               nodes.push({ ...event, name: event.label ?? event.name ?? event.id });\n2006:             } else if (event.type === 'edge') {\n2007:               edges.push({\n2008:                 ...event,\n2009:                 sourceId: event.sourceId ?? event.source,\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2010]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 1930-2009\n1930:           message: \"The {unavailable_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({unavailable_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1931:           halt: true\n1932:         if_absent:\n1933:           action: \"Continue to state reduction\"\n1934: \n1935:       step_reduce_state:\n1936:         action: \"Run the reducer to synchronize registry, dashboard, and strategy\"\n1937:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n1938:         inputs:\n1939:           latestJSONLDelta: \"Latest JSONL records written since the previous iteration\"\n1940:           newIterationFile: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1941:           priorReducedState: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1942:         outputs:\n1943:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1944:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1945:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1946:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} question_conflict events when inbox text disagrees with registry-owned question text\"\n1947:           - \"{state_paths.state_log} idempotent idea_promoted events when observed ideas reach minIdeaObservations\"\n1948:           - \"{state_paths.registry} observedIdeas, promotedIdeas, suppressedIdeas, rejectedPatterns, and suppressedCandidates from idea lifecycle events\"\n1949:         failure_modes:\n1950:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1951:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1952:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1953:           question_conflict: \"keep registry value + append question_conflict event with inboxValue, registryValue, and operatorDecision\"\n1954:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n1955: \n1956:       step_graph_upsert:\n1957:         action: \"Persist the latest iteration graph delta after the reducer refresh and after the iteration file exists\"\n1958:         note: \"Skips with an informational line and exit 0 when this iteration carries no graph events.\"\n1959:         command: |\n1960:           node <<'EOF'\n1961:           const { existsSync, readFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n1962:           const { join } = require('node:path');\n1963:           const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n1964: \n1965:           const deltaDir = '{state_paths.delta_dir}';\n1966:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n1967:           const iteration = Number('{current_iteration}');\n1968:           const specFolder = '{spec_folder}';\n1969:           const sessionId = '{config.lineage.sessionId}';\n1970: \n1971:           function parseJsonLines(raw, source) {\n1972:             const records = [];\n1973:             for (const line of raw.split(/\\r?\\n/)) {\n1974:               const trimmed = line.trim();\n1975:               if (!trimmed) continue;\n1976:               try {\n1977:                 records.push(JSON.parse(trimmed));\n1978:               } catch (error) {\n1979:                 process.stderr.write(`deep-research graph upsert: skipped malformed line in ${source}: ${error.message}\\n`);\n1980:               }\n1981:             }\n1982:             return records;\n1983:           }\n1984: \n1985:           function latestGraphEvents(records) {\n1986:             for (let index = records.length - 1; index >= 0; index -= 1) {\n1987:               const record = records[index];\n1988:               if (record && record.type === 'iteration') {\n1989:                 return Array.isArray(record.graphEvents) ? record.graphEvents : [];\n1990:               }\n1991:             }\n1992:             return [];\n1993:           }\n1994: \n1995:           const deltaPath = join(deltaDir, `iter-${String(iteration).padStart(3, '0')}.jsonl`);\n1996:           const sourcePath = existsSync(deltaPath) ? deltaPath : stateLogPath;\n1997:           const records = existsSync(sourcePath) ? parseJsonLines(readFileSync(sourcePath, 'utf8'), sourcePath) : [];\n1998:           const events = latestGraphEvents(records);\n1999: \n2000:           const nodes = [];\n2001:           const edges = [];\n2002:           for (const event of events) {\n2003:             if (!event || typeof event !== 'object') continue;\n2004:             if (event.type === 'node') {\n2005:               nodes.push({ ...event, name: event.label ?? event.name ?? event.id });\n2006:             } else if (event.type === 'edge') {\n2007:               edges.push({\n2008:                 ...event,\n2009:                 sourceId: event.sourceId ?? event.source,\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2010]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\",\"offset\":1930,\"limit\":80}"},"time":{"start":1794523733658,"end":1794523734478}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523734481,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f3204c001UoAf7E2s6MsOB8","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f31377001QY1KNqFZrT0zCj","type":"tool","id":"call_1293365e81ca4d7595a7e5db","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":2186,"limit":150},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 2186-2335\n2186:   phase_synthesis:\n2187:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into final research/research.md\n2188:     steps:\n2189: \n2190:       step_fanout_merge:\n2191:         description: \"Merge N lineage registries into one consolidated registry; skip when single-executor\"\n2192:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n2193:         command: |\n2194:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n2195:             --loop-type research \\\n2196:             --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n2197:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2198:         wait_for_completion: true\n2199: \n2200:       step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n2201:         action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n2202:         read:\n2203:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2204:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2205:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n2206:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2207:         read_patterns:\n2208:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n2209:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n2210:         extract:\n2211:           - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count distinct run values (run, else iteration) across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count distinct run values (run, else iteration) across the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2212:           - highest_run: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, take the highest run value (run, else iteration) across lines where type === 'iteration' in those logs in stable lineage order, else 0; otherwise take the highest run value (run, else iteration) across lines where type === 'iteration' in the root state log, else 0. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n2213:           - current_iteration: \"max(highest_run, iteration_count) + 1\"\n2214:           - current_segment: \"Latest segment_start event segment, else 1\"\n2215:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n2216:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newInfoRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2217:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newInfoRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n2218:           - remaining_questions: \"Count unchecked items in 'Key Questions'\"\n2219:           - remaining_questions_list: \"List unchecked key questions from strategy.md\"\n2220:           - answered_count: \"Count answered questions from strategy.md\"\n2221:           - total_questions: \"Count total questions tracked in strategy.md\"\n2222:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: focus (ratio)'\"\n2223:           - divergence_summary: \"Read registry.divergence and summarize saturated directions, completed pivots, failures, overrides, Council artifact refs, and remaining frontier; else 'no divergent pivots recorded'\"\n2224:           - reason: \"Use the latest synthesis/recovery stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n2225: \n2226:       step_read_all_iterations:\n2227:         action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n2228:         read_patterns:\n2229:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n2230:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/iterations/iteration-*.md\"\n2231:         read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n2232:         identity: \"Preserve each full source path and lineage label. Duplicate basenames from different lineages are distinct synthesis inputs; do not copy or renumber them.\"\n2233:         selection: \"When lineage iteration files exist, synthesize from those files in stable lineage-plus-iteration order; otherwise use root iterations.\"\n2234: \n2235:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2236:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged research deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2237:         branch_on: \"config.fanout\"\n2238:         if_present:\n2239:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map --fanout-resource-map-only\"\n2240:           read:\n2241:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2242:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2243:             - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deltas/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2244:         if_absent:\n2245:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} --emit-resource-map\"\n2246:           read:\n2247:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2248:             - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2249:         write:\n2250:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2251:         guarantee: \"Fan-out resource-map emission reads lineage deltas in place and writes only resource-map.md; it never rewrites merged registries, strategy, or dashboard. Single-executor reduction remains unchanged.\"\n2252: \n2253:       step_compile_research:\n2254:         action: \"Compile or finalize research/research.md\"\n2255:         instructions: |\n2256:           If research/research.md exists (progressive synthesis was active):\n2257:             1. Read current research/research.md\n2258:             2. Consolidate and deduplicate findings across all iterations\n2259:             3. Fill any empty sections with findings from iteration files\n2260:             4. Remove redundancy while preserving all unique findings\n2261:             5. Add convergence report as appendix\n2262:             6. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2263:             7. Preserve the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section, then add or replace `## Divergence Map` immediately after it and before Section 12 Open Questions. Populate it from `{state_paths.registry}` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier.\n2264: \n2265:           If research/research.md does not exist:\n2266:             1. Create research/research.md following 17-section template\n2267:             2. Populate sections from iteration files\n2268:             3. Add citations from original sources\n2269:             4. Note unanswered questions in Open Questions section\n2270:             5. If `resource_map_present` is true, cite `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` in References; otherwise omit any placeholder map citation\n2271:             6. After the mandatory `## Eliminated Alternatives` section and before Section 12 Open Questions, add `## Divergence Map` with saturated directions, pivots taken, evidence and Council artifact references, pivot failures and audited overrides, and the remaining frontier from `{state_paths.registry}`.\n2272:           Divergence Map documents breadth. Never claim the topic converged merely because divergent mode broadened the investigated frontier.\n2273:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract`.)\n2274:         output: \"{state_paths.research_output}\"\n2275: \n2276:       step_convergence_report:\n2277:         action: \"Generate and append convergence report\"\n2278:         report: |\n2279:           ## Convergence Report\n2280:           - Stop reason: {reason}\n2281:           - Total iterations: {iteration_count}\n2282:           - Questions answered: {answered_count} / {total_questions}\n2283:           - Remaining questions: {remaining_questions}\n2284:           - Last 3 iteration summaries: {last_3_summaries}\n2285:           - Convergence threshold: {convergence_threshold}\n2286:           - Divergence summary: {divergence_summary}\n2287:           - Segment transitions, wave scores, and checkpoint metrics are experimental and omitted from the live report.\n2288:         command: |\n2289:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2290:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2291:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2292:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2293:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2294:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode research --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2295:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2296:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2297:             --registry \"{state_paths.registry}\" \\\n2298:             --output \"{state_paths.research_output}\" \\\n2299:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2300:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2301:             --answered-count \"{answered_count}\" --total-questions \"{total_questions}\"\n2302:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2303:           for 