easure command routing before changing it: a command prompt corpus and a baseline for the 44 tracked commands.\n79: - Generate one command inventory with a risk class and a derived policy per command and per doctor route.\n80: - Make plain chat reach a command: attach the command to its owner skill for hub commands, and author intent phrases for commands with no hub mode.\n81: - Reach a command from a paraphrase that shares no words with it, by matching the prompt's meaning against a vector per command.\n82: - Extend the recommendation and the brief with the command, its policy and its owner skill.\n83: - Bind the behaviour in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 and in a generated pointer for runtimes with no brief.\n84: - Prove the behaviour per runtime from transcripts.\n85: \n86: ### Out of Scope\n87: - Changing how skills are scored against each other. The four existing accuracy numbers are a floor in every phase.\n88: - Surfacing the private, untracked `/local-skilled-alignment` command (decision D5).\n89: - Forcing the command path. Decision D2 keeps the model free to pick the skill path.\n90: - Adding a command front door to a skill that has none.\n91: \n92: ### Files to Change\n93: Audit trail only. Each child's `plan.md` holds the detail, and phases 5 to 7 are not planned yet, so their rows name the area the review points at.\n94: \n95: | File Path | Change Type | Phase | Description |\n96: |-----------|-------------|-------|-------------|\n97: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/` | Create | 001 | Command prompt corpus, its scorer and a baseline file |\n98: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/` | Modify | 002 | One generated inventory, risk class and policy, retired ids |\n99: | `.skilled/skills/*/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` | Modify, Create | 002 | Risk class and write target per command and route |\n100: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/`, `advisor/handlers/` | Modify | 003 | Command attached to the owner skill, authored phrases, one row per command |\n101: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/`, `lib/skill-graph/`, `scripts/command-bridges/`, `scripts/routing-accuracy/` | Modify | 004 | A vector per command, a meaning anchor in scoring and a capture that uses the real embedding |\n102: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `lib/render.ts` | Modify | 005 | New recommendation fields and the brief line |\n103: | `AGENTS.md`, generated runtime pointer blocks | Modify | 006 | The Gate 2 sentence, the Gate 4 retirement and the static pointer |\n104: | Per-runtime transcript checks | Create | 007 | Behaviour proof and the started-command-is-followed check |\n105: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n110: ## PHASE DOCUMENTATION MAP\n111: \n112: > This spec uses phased decomposition. Each phase is an independently executable child spec folder. All implementation details (plan, tasks, checklist, decisions, continuity) live inside the phase children.\n113: \n114: | Phase | Folder | Focus | Status |\n115: |-------|--------|-------|--------|\n116: | 1 | 001-command-routing-baseline-corpus/ | Command prompt corpus and baseline, no scorer change (R8, L8, L9) | Complete |\n117: | 2 | 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/ | One generated inventory, risk class and derived policy, private command excluded (R1, R4, G4) | Complete |\n118: | 3 | 003-plain-chat-command-reach/ | Attach commands to owner skills, authored phrases, one activation source (R2, L2, L3, R10 precedence) | Complete |\n119: | 4 | 004-command-meaning-matching/ | A vector per command and a meaning anchor, so a paraphrase reaches its command (operator decision, 2026-11-12) | Complete |\n120: | 5 | 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/ | Recommendation fields, brief line, degraded path, retired ids (R3, L6, L12, G6, L1, L7) | Pending |\n121: | 6 | 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/ | Gate 2 sentence, typed override, static pointer, child authority (R6, L5, R5, L4, G1, G3, L10) | Pending |\n122: | 7 | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/ | Transcript proof per runtime and the started-command-is-followed check (R8 transcripts, G2, G5) | Pending |\n123: | 8 | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/ | The embedder for external repositories: visible state, a plan-first doctor route, the measured memory and latency cost in the install guides and defined absent, cold and slow behaviour (operator requirement, 2026-11-12) | Pending |\n124: \n125: ### Phase Transition Rules\n126: \n127: - Each phase MUST pass `validate.sh` independently before the next phase begins\n128: - Parent spec tracks aggregate progress via this map\n129: - Use `/speckit:resume [parent-folder]/[NNN-phase]/` to resume a specific phase\n130: - Run `validate.sh --recursive` on parent to validate all phases as integrated unit\n131: \n132: ### Phase Handoff Criteria\n133: \n134: | From | To | Criteria | Verification |\n135: |------|-----|----------|--------------|\n136: | 001-command-routing-baseline-corpus | 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | Corpus rows exist for all 44 tracked commands and a baseline records per-command recall, with the four existing numbers unchanged | The baseline file exists and the existing routing-accuracy run still reports 158/195, 50/66 and 20/24 |\n137: | 002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | Every tracked command and doctor route has a risk class and a derived policy | The deriver's check mode is fresh and exits 1 on a fixture command with no metadata |\n138: | 003-plain-chat-command-reach | 004-command-meaning-matching | Command recall rises against the phase 1 baseline with no drop in the four existing numbers | The phase 1 scorer run, and no typed command is ambiguous with its own owner |\n139: | 004-command-meaning-matching | 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief | Holdout plain recall rises above 0 of 44 with false offers at 0 of 35 and typed recall at least 24 of 44, measured with the real embedding | The real-embedding capture and the full advisor suite |\n140: | 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief | 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | The recommendation and the brief carry the command and its policy | Schema test and golden briefs pass, and `save context` returns one entry |\n141: | 006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | The Gate 2 sentence and the generated pointer are in place | `/doctor:agents-md check` passes and the pointer generator's check exits 0 |\n142: | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost | Phase 005 is merged and the per-runtime proof is recorded, so this phase edits the final recommendation handler and bridge activation list | `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line and phase 007 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-map -->\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n148: ## 4. OPEN QUESTIONS\n149: \n150: - Phase 7 needs runs on runtimes the research never exercised live (Pi, Cursor, Devin, DSH, Codex, OpenCode). Which of them the operator wants proven is decided when phase 7 is planned.\n151: - The review's G2 check, that a started command actually runs its own setup, is a condition of decision D1. If phase 7 shows setup being skipped, D1 returns to the operator.\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: ## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n157: \n158: - **Phase children**: See sub-folders `[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` for per-phase spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md\n159: - **Parent Spec**: See `../spec.md`\n160: - **Graph Metadata**: See `graph-metadata.json` for `derived.last_active_child_id` pointer"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523753960,"end":1794523754501}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794523756412,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f3777c001KCVxwbq6NyhkOC","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f365d6001V99XZ7EgO51z5L","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"410b613c128f46ccb40f0c38783beca26d7dcfe3","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":774,"output":109,"reasoning":31,"cache":{"read":63616,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794523758135,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f37e37001V6VTK4cNzVaa4J","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f37781001ZCUN4guWO4rPg2","type":"step-start","snapshot":"aaccd0de0e2181f3324846b4441a6b18123f0927"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523759246,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f38001001nSQ6X5r2i6k3ox","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f37781001ZCUN4guWO4rPg2","type":"tool","id":"call_aff214e6fdd84148a13f7aaf","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 1-173\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and its hooks |\n25: | **Storage** | None. The command table is generated source, and the bridge file is JSON |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four design questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog, each the recommended option, and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n40: - [ ] The coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done. No code task starts before it.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the pinned capture, the default command capture, the rollup, six live brief heads, the sk-doc reach check, three hook timing runs and the suite.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] The schema test, the six golden briefs and the reach check with real embeddings pass. `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: One generated table, many readers. Nothing hand-keeps a command string or a policy.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n59: - **Public fields** (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): `publicRecommendation` copies `kind` and, for a row found in `COMMAND_ROWS`, sets `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. `enrichCompiledRoutes` adds the policy of an attached command and reads the already-offered set from the `command` fields instead of from bridge keywords.\n60: - **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n61: - **Degraded contract** (`ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`): `degradedRecommendations` keeps a command row's fields only when its bare slash command appears in the prompt, and otherwise replaces it with its owner skill.\n62: - **Reach check** (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`): `rankShippedFleet` counts a hit when the first shipped entry is the hub or is a command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the hub.\n63: \n64: ### Data Flow\n65: `command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n113: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n114: \n115: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n116: |-----------|-------|-------|\n117: | Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n118: | Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n119: | Manual | `save context`, `/speckit:plan` and readme CLI checks, six live hook heads, the reach check with Ollama, three hook timing runs | The advisor CLI, the phase 003 timing script copied into `scratch/` |\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n126: \n127: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n128: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n129: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` | Internal | Green: generated today | No policy to show |\n130: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the `command` field | Internal | Green: in code today | No attached command to label |\n131: | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text` | External | Green: the tags call listed `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on 2026-11-12 | The reach proof for REQ-018 cannot run |\n132: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n133: | Phase 007 before-measurement on the branch tip | Ordering | Open: waits on the coordinator's confirmation | Every code task waits, wave 0 may run |\n134: | The `nm-sk-doc-01` source trace | Internal | Open: the token sources are UNKNOWN until T055 | The fix task T056 cannot name its file |\n135: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n140: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n141: \n142: - **Trigger**: a pinned number moves, a default capture number moves, a false offer appears or the suite fails after the waves that touch scoring ids.\n143: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits, run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `npm run build` in `ADV`. Then confirm `--check` prints `fresh` and the pinned capture prints `[159,50,20,5]`. The id rename and the relabel revert together because they land in the same commits.\n144: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n150: \n151: ```\n152: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n153: ```\n154: \n155: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n156: |-------|------------|--------|\n157: | Setup | Phase 004 shipped code | Implementation |\n158: | Implementation | The before numbers, the operator answers and the phase 007 confirmation | Verification |\n159: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 006 |\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n165: ## DECISIONS ALREADY MADE\n166: \n167: No new decision is recorded here. The phase follows these, all in `../decision-record.md` or the review:\n168: - D1 (Q006): a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started. The `start` word in the head carries it.\n169: - D2 (Q007, Q011): the model picks freely between the command and the skill. The head names both.\n170: - The review's R3 field set and the L12 rule of no consequence line, read in `synthesis-review.md` section 3.\n171: \n172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 1-173\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and its hooks |\n25: | **Storage** | None. The command table is generated source, and the bridge file is JSON |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four design questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog, each the recommended option, and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n40: - [ ] The coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done. No code task starts before it.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the pinned capture, the default command capture, the rollup, six live brief heads, the sk-doc reach check, three hook timing runs and the suite.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] The schema test, the six golden briefs and the reach check with real embeddings pass. `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: One generated table, many readers. Nothing hand-keeps a command string or a policy.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n59: - **Public fields** (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): `publicRecommendation` copies `kind` and, for a row found in `COMMAND_ROWS`, sets `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. `enrichCompiledRoutes` adds the policy of an attached command and reads the already-offered set from the `command` fields instead of from bridge keywords.\n60: - **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n61: - **Degraded contract** (`ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`): `degradedRecommendations` keeps a command row's fields only when its bare slash command appears in the prompt, and otherwise replaces it with its owner skill.\n62: - **Reach check** (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`): `rankShippedFleet` counts a hit when the first shipped entry is the hub or is a command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the hub.\n63: \n64: ### Data Flow\n65: `command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n113: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n114: \n115: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n116: |-----------|-------|-------|\n117: | Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n118: | Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n119: | Manual | `save context`, `/speckit:plan` and readme CLI checks, six live hook heads, the reach check with Ollama, three hook timing runs | The advisor CLI, the phase 003 timing script copied into `scratch/` |\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n126: \n127: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n128: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n129: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` | Internal | Green: generated today | No policy to show |\n130: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the `command` field | Internal | Green: in code today | No attached command to label |\n131: | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text` | External | Green: the tags call listed `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on 2026-11-12 | The reach proof for REQ-018 cannot run |\n132: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n133: | Phase 007 before-measurement on the branch tip | Ordering | Open: waits on the coordinator's confirmation | Every code task waits, wave 0 may run |\n134: | The `nm-sk-doc-01` source trace | Internal | Open: the token sources are UNKNOWN until T055 | The fix task T056 cannot name its file |\n135: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n140: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n141: \n142: - **Trigger**: a pinned number moves, a default capture number moves, a false offer appears or the suite fails after the waves that touch scoring ids.\n143: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits, run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `npm run build` in `ADV`. Then confirm `--check` prints `fresh` and the pinned capture prints `[159,50,20,5]`. The id rename and the relabel revert together because they land in the same commits.\n144: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n150: \n151: ```\n152: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n153: ```\n154: \n155: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n156: |-------|------------|--------|\n157: | Setup | Phase 004 shipped code | Implementation |\n158: | Implementation | The before numbers, the operator answers and the phase 007 confirmation | Verification |\n159: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 006 |\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n165: ## DECISIONS ALREADY MADE\n166: \n167: No new decision is recorded here. The phase follows these, all in `../decision-record.md` or the review:\n168: - D1 (Q006): a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started. The `start` word in the head carries it.\n169: - D2 (Q007, Q011): the model picks freely between the command and the skill. The head names both.\n170: - The review's R3 field set and the L12 rule of no consequence line, read in `synthesis-review.md` section 3.\n171: \n172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523758593,"end":1794523759246}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523759250,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f3813c001mwkfX26vkVgYtM","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f37781001ZCUN4guWO4rPg2","type":"tool","id":"call_030080d1ebc54bb18db6803b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 1-256\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Add one Gate 2 bullet for a surfaced command, copy it into the Cursor rule through the existing pointer generator, hand a hub mode to its command, name the plan workflow in the Gate 3 notice and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Markdown instruction files, CommonJS generators, one ES module, one Bash script and TypeScript in the advisor |\n24: | **Framework** | The `AGENTS.md` manifest and check engine under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, the spec-kit runtime mirrors and the system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV`) |\n25: | **Storage** | None. Every output is a tracked text file |\n26: | **Testing** | `/doctor:agents-md check`, the manifest check, the rule-copy canary, Vitest in `ADV` and in the spec-kit CLI, `node --test` for the spec gate |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The rule lives once, in Gate 2 of `AGENTS.md`. Every other surface either copies it through a generator that checks the copy, or points at the command document from where a model already is: the hub router after it picks a mode, the Gate 3 notice before the first write and the brief in a child session. Nothing in scoring moves.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12. `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 shipped, and the Claude hook's first line for `create a readme for the utils folder` shows `/create:readme` and a policy word (T002). Without it only the REQ-004 tasks wait.\n40: - [ ] The before numbers in `spec.md` Measured Behavior still hold (T001).\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `/doctor:agents-md check` prints `STATUS=OK`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n128: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n129: \n130: - **Trigger**: `/doctor:agents-md check` not `OK`, the pointer check failing, a failing suite or a behaviour run in phase 007 showing the bullet steers turns wrongly.\n131: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commit, then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` so the derived copy and the Cursor rule match the reverted `AGENTS.md`. Finish with `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n132: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n133: \n134: ---\n135: \n136: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n137: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n138: \n139: ```\n140: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n141: ```\n142: \n143: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n144: |-------|------------|--------|\n145: | Setup | Operator answers, phase 005 for REQ-004 only | Implementation |\n146: | Implementation | The before numbers | Verification |\n147: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 007 |\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n153: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n154: \n155: Every ADR below records an operator decision already made. None is new.\n156: \n157: ### ADR-001: The command path and the skill path are both whole workflows\n158: \n159: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Looser: AI picks freely\" (`../decision-record.md` Q011, D2)\n160: \n161: **Context**: The review's Gate 2 text and its G1 router rule make the command the workflow a model must follow.\n162: \n163: **Decision**: The Gate 2 bullet and the three router bullets name the command beside the skill. A model picks either and follows it whole, never an improvised mix. The operator approved the exact Gate 2 text on 2026-11-12, \"Command beside the skill (Recommended)\".\n164: \n165: **Consequences**:\n166: - The command is a suggestion the model may decline. The `COMMAND:` token records `declined` so phase 007 can count it.\n167: - A `command: null` mode keeps its packet as the only path.\n168: \n169: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n170: - Command as the default entry with the skill for partial work: the operator chose the looser reading over it (Q011).\n171: \n172: ### ADR-002: A started command runs without `:auto`\n173: \n174: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Start it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q006, D1)\n175: \n176: **Context**: Twenty commands carry the `start` policy, and their own setup asks for a mode, Gate 3 and a yes at an irreversible step.\n177: \n178: **Decision**: The bullet defines `start` as starting the command without `:auto`, so its setup asks.\n179: \n180: **Consequences**:\n181: - A typed `:auto` or an explicit instruction still wins (L5).\n182: - Whether a started command keeps to its setup is phase 007's G2 check.\n183: \n184: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n185: - Ask before every write command: rejected by the operator (Q006).\n186: \n187: ### ADR-003: A deep loop is always asked first\n188: \n189: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Only on depth wording (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q008, D3)\n190: \n191: **Context**: The three `/deep:*` commands carry the `ask` policy in `commandPolicies` today.\n192: \n193: **Decision**: The bullet's `ask` sentence covers them, and no deep-loop clause is added to `AGENTS.md`. The deep-loop router bullet notes that `deep-research/SKILL.md` names its command as its only entry.\n194: \n195: **Consequences**:\n196: - No bytes spent on a deep-loop rule in the delivery prefix.\n197: \n198: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n199: - A separate deep-loop clause in Gate 2: it would restate the policy word.\n200: \n201: ### ADR-004: The invocation table covers the 44 tracked commands\n202: \n203: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"No, exclude it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q012, D5)\n204: \n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n255: - Keep the label with a retired list: the operator chose removal.\n256: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 1-256\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Add one Gate 2 bullet for a surfaced command, copy it into the Cursor rule through the existing pointer generator, hand a hub mode to its command, name the plan workflow in the Gate 3 notice and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Markdown instruction files, CommonJS generators, one ES module, one Bash script and TypeScript in the advisor |\n24: | **Framework** | The `AGENTS.md` manifest and check engine under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, the spec-kit runtime mirrors and the system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV`) |\n25: | **Storage** | None. Every output is a tracked text file |\n26: | **Testing** | `/doctor:agents-md check`, the manifest check, the rule-copy canary, Vitest in `ADV` and in the spec-kit CLI, `node --test` for the spec gate |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The rule lives once, in Gate 2 of `AGENTS.md`. Every other surface either copies it through a generator that checks the copy, or points at the command document from where a model already is: the hub router after it picks a mode, the Gate 3 notice before the first write and the brief in a child session. Nothing in scoring moves.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12. `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 shipped, and the Claude hook's first line for `create a readme for the utils folder` shows `/create:readme` and a policy word (T002). Without it only the REQ-004 tasks wait.\n40: - [ ] The before numbers in `spec.md` Measured Behavior still hold (T001).\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `/doctor:agents-md check` prints `STATUS=OK`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n128: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n129: \n130: - **Trigger**: `/doctor:agents-md check` not `OK`, the pointer check failing, a failing suite or a behaviour run in phase 007 showing the bullet steers turns wrongly.\n131: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commit, then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` so the derived copy and the Cursor rule match the reverted `AGENTS.md`. Finish with `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n132: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n133: \n134: ---\n135: \n136: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n137: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n138: \n139: ```\n140: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n141: ```\n142: \n143: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n144: |-------|------------|--------|\n145: | Setup | Operator answers, phase 005 for REQ-004 only | Implementation |\n146: | Implementation | The before numbers | Verification |\n147: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 007 |\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n153: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n154: \n155: Every ADR below records an operator decision already made. None is new.\n156: \n157: ### ADR-001: The command path and the skill path are both whole workflows\n158: \n159: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Looser: AI picks freely\" (`../decision-record.md` Q011, D2)\n160: \n161: **Context**: The review's Gate 2 text and its G1 router rule make the command the workflow a model must follow.\n162: \n163: **Decision**: The Gate 2 bullet and the three router bullets name the command beside the skill. A model picks either and follows it whole, never an improvised mix. The operator approved the exact Gate 2 text on 2026-11-12, \"Command beside the skill (Recommended)\".\n164: \n165: **Consequences**:\n166: - The command is a suggestion the model may decline. The `COMMAND:` token records `declined` so phase 007 can count it.\n167: - A `command: null` mode keeps its packet as the only path.\n168: \n169: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n170: - Command as the default entry with the skill for partial work: the operator chose the looser reading over it (Q011).\n171: \n172: ### ADR-002: A started command runs without `:auto`\n173: \n174: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Start it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q006, D1)\n175: \n176: **Context**: Twenty commands carry the `start` policy, and their own setup asks for a mode, Gate 3 and a yes at an irreversible step.\n177: \n178: **Decision**: The bullet defines `start` as starting the command without `:auto`, so its setup asks.\n179: \n180: **Consequences**:\n181: - A typed `:auto` or an explicit instruction still wins (L5).\n182: - Whether a started command keeps to its setup is phase 007's G2 check.\n183: \n184: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n185: - Ask before every write command: rejected by the operator (Q006).\n186: \n187: ### ADR-003: A deep loop is always asked first\n188: \n189: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Only on depth wording (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q008, D3)\n190: \n191: **Context**: The three `/deep:*` commands carry the `ask` policy in `commandPolicies` today.\n192: \n193: **Decision**: The bullet's `ask` sentence covers them, and no deep-loop clause is added to `AGENTS.md`. The deep-loop router bullet notes that `deep-research/SKILL.md` names its command as its only entry.\n194: \n195: **Consequences**:\n196: - No bytes spent on a deep-loop rule in the delivery prefix.\n197: \n198: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n199: - A separate deep-loop clause in Gate 2: it would restate the policy word.\n200: \n201: ### ADR-004: The invocation table covers the 44 tracked commands\n202: \n203: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"No, exclude it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q012, D5)\n204: \n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n255: - Keep the label with a retired list: the operator chose removal.\n256: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523758908,"end":1794523759250}}}}
