rs are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n78:- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n87:- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n88:- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n89:- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n97:- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n98:- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n== specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md\n2:- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$X/before.txt`). Verify: `M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, a plain block with tune combined 9 and holdout combined 0, and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `P` prints `[159,50,20,5]`, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`.\n3:- [x] T002 Record the pre-change commit (`$X/pre-change-commit.txt`). Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD > $X/pre-change-commit.txt` writes one 40-character SHA, and `rg -c \"COMMAND:\" AGENTS.md` exits 1 on that commit. If it exits 0, phase 005 has landed early: stop and ask the operator.\n4:- [x] T003 Record the CLI version of each measured runtime (`$X/cli-versions.txt`). No model call. Verify: the file holds one line per runtime for the six measured runtimes, each from that CLI's `--version`.\n12:- [x] T004 Create `S` with the CLI shell: flags `--runtime`, `--locator <json>`, `--row-id`, `--summary <run-log>` and `--json`, a call to `loadSession` from `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs`, and exit 2 with the reader's `code` on `ok: false`. Verify: `node $S --runtime cursor --locator '{\"sessionId\":\"x\"}'` exits 2 and prints `capability_gated`.\n13:- [x] T005 In `S`, add `normalize(records, runtime)`, which turns each record into `{seq, kind, path, command, text}` with `kind` one of `read`, `write`, `shell`, `skill` or `text`, using one tool-name table per runtime that starts from the sets in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/measure-rule-compliance.py`. A shell command counts as a write when it redirects into a file or runs `apply_patch`. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.normalize))\"` prints `function`.\n14:- [x] T006 In `S`, add `commandLines(events)`, which returns every assistant line matching `COMMAND: /<name> → <started|offered|declined>` with its count per command. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.commandLines))\"` prints `function`.\n15:- [x] T007 In `S`, add `followedBeforeWrite(events, command)`, true when a `read` or `skill` event names the command's document, and its confirm workflow file when it has one, before the first `write`. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.followedBeforeWrite))\"` prints `function`.\n16:- [x] T008 In `S`, add `startState(events, row)`, which returns `started`, `unsafe` and `selfAuto` per the definitions in `plan.md` section 3, joining the row's `expected_policy` and `row_type`. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.startState))\"` prints `function`.\n17:- [x] T009 In `S`, add `loopInit(events, command)`. For `/deep:research` and `/deep:review` it is false when a write under a `research/` or `review/` folder, or a `fanout-run.cjs` call, comes before a `loop-lock.cjs acquire` call. For `/speckit:complete` it is false when a write outside `specs/` comes before `create.sh` or a `spec.md` write. It returns `null` when the run started no loop. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.loopInit))\"` prints `function`.\n18:- [x] T010 In `S`, implement `--summary <run-log>`: per runtime and arm, the start rate as n of the `run` and `start` rows, the `COMMAND:` line rate, the unsafe count, the count of commands with more than one `COMMAND:` line, loops without init and unscored runs with their reasons. Verify: `node $S --summary /dev/null --json` exits 0 and prints `{}`.\n19:- [x] T011 Create `R` with the `RUNTIMES` table from `plan.md` section 3: one argv builder per runtime, each taken from that runtime's `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-*/SKILL.md` defaults, plus a 300 s cap for chat runs and a 900 s cap for started-command runs. Verify: `node $R --print-argv claude` prints an argv that holds `-p` and `stream-json`, and `node $R --print-argv cursor` exits 2.\n20:- [x] T012 In `R`, run each prompt with stdin from `/dev/null` and `AI_SESSION_CHILD` removed from the environment (operator approval of 2026-11-12), record `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` before and after, restore each tracked path that changed during the run with `git checkout --` and delete each untracked path the run created, then append `{runtime, rowId, arm, locator, exit, changedPaths, restored}` to `--out`. Two guards protect work that is not the run's own. Before the first prompt, `R` exits 2 with `worktree_dirty` when `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` lists any path outside this phase's `scratch/` folder, so a restore can never discard another worker's uncommitted edit. Before and after each prompt, `R` records `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD` and the output of `git -c core.fsmonitor=false stash list`, and when either changed it writes `headMoved: true` on the line, skips the restore and exits 3 without running another prompt. Verify: with one tracked file edited, `node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id <first tune start id> --out $X/dry.jsonl` exits 2 and prints `worktree_dirty`. On a clean tree, `node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id <first tune start id> --out $X/dry.jsonl` appends one line with `changedPaths` `[]`, and `rg -n \"AI_SESSION_CHILD\" $R` shows only the delete.\n21:- [x] T013 In `R`, add `--set chat` and `--set g2`. `chat` reads `command-prompts.jsonl`, refuses with exit 2 any row whose `split` is `holdout` before reading its prompt, and picks by sorted id the first 8 `start`, 4 `run` and 4 `ask` tune plain rows and the first 8 must-not-start rows. `g2` holds six fixed prompts: a natural ask and a typed `:auto` command for each of `/deep:research`, `/deep:review` and `/speckit:complete`, the two deep loops capped at one iteration, all aimed at `$X/g2-fixture/`. Verify: `node $R --list chat | wc -l` prints 24, `node $R --list g2 | wc -l` prints 6, and `node $R --row-id <any holdout id>` exits 2 without printing prompt text.\n22:- [x] T014 In `R`, capture the locator per runtime: Claude Code `session_id` from the stream, OpenCode `sessionID` from the events, Codex the thread id from `--json`, DSH the id the runner passes with `--session-id` and its `DSH_HOME`. Pi and Devin keep `UNKNOWN` until T022 records their locator source. Verify: `rg -n \"UNKNOWN\" $R` lists only the Pi and Devin rows.\n23:- [x] T015 Create `T` with built sessions in the projected record shape, one per runtime, and cases for: 0, 1 and 2 `COMMAND:` lines, a document read before and after the first write, each policy with and without a write, a self-chosen `:auto`, a deep loop with and without `loop-lock.cjs acquire`, a refused `fanout-run.cjs` call, `/speckit:complete` with and without a spec folder first and a reader failure. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n24:- [x] T047 Create `A` with flags `--source <repo root>` and `--dest <dir>`. It exits 2 with `dest_exists` when `--dest` exists and with `dest_in_repo` when `git -C <parent of dest> rev-parse --show-toplevel` succeeds. Otherwise it runs `git clone --no-hardlinks <source> <dest>`, checks out the source's current commit as a detached HEAD, removes every remote from the clone, then copies from the source every directory named `dist` or `node_modules` and every `*.sqlite` file that sits under `.skilled/` and is ignored by git, to the same relative path, with `cp -Rc`. It never copies a dotenv file, meaning any file whose name starts with a dot followed by `env`. It prints one JSON line `{ok, dest, head, copied}`. Verify: with `D=\"$TMPDIR/arena-check-$$\"`, `node $A --source . --dest \"$D\"` prints `ok: true` with `head` equal to `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD`, `git -C \"$D\" remote` prints nothing, `git -C \"$D\" status --porcelain` prints nothing, `node \"$D/.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\" advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json` prints a recommendation, a second run with the same `--dest` exits 2 with `dest_exists`, and `rm -rf \"$D\"` removes it.\n25:- [x] T048 In `R`, harden a live turn against acting outside its checkout. In `childEnv()`, delete `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN`, set `GH_CONFIG_DIR` to an empty folder the runner creates beside the run log, set `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT` to `0`, and set `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` to `1` with `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0` `credential.helper` and `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0` empty. Before the first prompt of a run that is not `--dry-run`, `R` exits 2 with `remote_present` when `git -c core.fsmonitor=false remote` prints any name, so a live turn can only start in a checkout that has no remote. Verify: `node $R --runtime claude --row-id mns-chat-01 --out $X/remote-check.jsonl` run from this worktree exits 2 and prints `remote_present` without starting a session, `node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id mns-chat-01 --out $X/dry.jsonl` still gets past that check, and `rg -n \"GH_CONFIG_DIR|credential.helper|GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT\" $R` prints three or more lines.\n26:- [x] T049 In `S`, let the `COMMAND_LINE` pattern accept markup around the command name and around the state word: an optional backtick, an optional square bracket or both on each side, so ``COMMAND: `/create:readme` → started`` and `COMMAND: [/create:readme] → [started]` both count as one line for `/create:readme`. In `T`, add one case for each of those two spellings and one case proving that `COMMAND: /create:readme → maybe` is still not counted. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and 42 or more passed.\n27:- [x] T050 In `R`, make every locator carry the checkout the turn ran in. `locatorFor` adds `projectDir`, the real path of `REPO_ROOT` from `fs.realpathSync`, to the object it returns for every runtime, because each session reader finds a stored session by `sessionId` plus `projectDir` and the scorer runs from a different checkout. A locator that has no session id stays as it is today. Verify: `node --check $R` passes and `rg -n \"projectDir\" $R` prints two or more lines.\n28:- [x] T051 In `R`, deliver the prompt on stdin for a runtime whose table row has `promptOnStdin: true` (codex and dsh). `spawnTurn` takes the prompt, opens stdin as a pipe for those runtimes, writes the prompt and ends the stream. Every other runtime keeps stdin ignored. The first smoke run failed here: codex printed `No prompt provided via stdin.` and dsh printed `a task is required`. Verify: `node --check $R` passes, `rg -n \"stdin.end\\(\" $R` prints one line, and `node $R --print-argv codex` still ends with `-`.\n29:- [x] T052 In `R`, correct the OpenCode argv for opencode 2.2.7, whose `run` command has no `--variant` and no `--dir` flag. Remove both flags and their values. Pass the variant inside the model string as `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max`. Keep `run`, `--model`, `--format json`, `--auto` and the prompt as the last argument. The turn already starts with the checkout as its working directory. Verify: `node $R --print-argv opencode` prints no `--variant` and no `--dir` and holds `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max`.\n30:- [x] T053 In `R`, give Pi a session id the runner mints. Add `--session-id` followed by the runner's `sessionId` to the Pi argv and set the Pi row's locator to `{ kind: 'runner' }`, the way the dsh row does. Remove the comment that says Pi's locator is not known. Verify: `node $R --print-argv pi` holds `--session-id`, and `rg -n \"UNKNOWN\" $R` lists only the Devin row.\n31:- [x] T054 In `R`, make Devin runnable in an arena and find its session. Add `--respect-workspace-trust false` to the Devin argv, before the `--` separator. Do not add `--sandbox`: it forces a permission mode that rejects every write in print mode, as the fan-out runner records. The first smoke run failed with `Refusing to run in an untrusted workspace`. For the locator, run `devin list --format json` with the checkout as working directory before and after the turn, and record as `sessionId` the one session id that is in the second list and not in the first. When there is none or more than one, the locator stays without a session id. Verify: `node $R --print-argv devin` holds `--respect-workspace-trust` and `false` and no `--sandbox`, and `rg -n \"UNKNOWN\" $R` prints nothing.\n32:- [x] T055 In `R`, add `transcriptPath` to the Claude Code and Codex locators, because `loadClaudeSession` and `loadCodexSession` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/` open a session by `sessionId` plus `transcriptPath` and answer `locator_unavailable` without it. After the turn, for Claude Code find the file named `<sessionId>.jsonl` in a direct child folder of `<CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.claude>/projects/`. For Codex find the file whose name ends with `-<sessionId>.jsonl` anywhere under `<CODEX_HOME or ~/.codex>/sessions/`. When exactly one file matches, record its absolute path as `transcriptPath`. Otherwise leave the field out. Verify: `node --check $R` passes and `rg -n \"transcriptPath\" $R` prints two or more lines.\n33:- [x] T056 In `R`, let DSH create its own session. The second smoke run failed with `session ... does not exist; omit --session-id to start a new Session`. Remove `--session-id` and its value from the DSH argv. Set the DSH row's locator to a store listing: before and after the turn, list the directory names in `<DSH_HOME or ~/.dsh>/sessions/<key>/`, where `<key>` is `dshProjectKey(projectDir)` imported from `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs`, and record as `sessionId` the one name that is in the second list and not in the first. A missing folder counts as an empty list. When there is none or more than one, the locator stays without a session id. Keep `dshHome` and `projectDir` on the locator. Also stop adding `dshHome` to the Pi locator. Verify: `node $R --print-argv dsh` holds no `--session-id` and still ends with `-`, and `node --check $R` passes.\n34:- [x] T057 In `S`, score a run whenever its session loads, whatever its exit code. Today `--summary` counts a run with a non-zero exit as unscored with reason `exit_<code>`, which threw away the OpenCode smoke run that worked for five minutes and was stopped by the cap. A run is unscored only when it has no usable locator or the reader fails, and the reason is then the reader's code. Add a `capped` count per runtime and arm for runs whose exit is 143 or null. In `T`, add a case where a run with exit 143 and a loadable session is scored and counted as capped, and a case where a run with exit 1 and no session id is unscored. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and 44 or more passed.\n35:- [x] T016 [P] Document both scripts, their flags and exit 2 in `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`. Verify: `rg -n \"score-command-transcripts|run-command-behaviour\" $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` prints at least two lines.\n36:- [x] T017 In `doctorLeadPhrases` (`D`), reject a lead phrase that holds no state or health word (`check`, `state`, `status`, `report`, `health`, `off`, `on`, `which`, `show`, `list`, `inventory`, `drift`, `stale`, `missing`, `failing`, `broken`) unless its route's derived policy is `ask`. Verify: `node $D --check` p