sor.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"embedder\" DOC/skill-advisor.md` prints at least two lines.\n10:- [ ] T019 Create the degrade test with the adapter, the active pointer and the read-only database mocked, and `VITEST` stubbed to `false` inside each case. Six rows: warm answer scored with a cosine, cold answer at 300 ms scored with a cosine, absent server, missing model, an answer that never arrives, which returns inside `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS` plus 100 ms, and a failure that leaves the result equal to the no-embedder result. Each failure row checks its `disabledReason` (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 6 passed.\n11:- [ ] T020 Add the route's activation entry to both the `typescript` and the `python` lists, copying the shape of the `command-doctor-skill-advisor-router-reach` entries, then run `node $D` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`). Verify: `node $D --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n12:- [ ] T021 Add `export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[]`, which returns a one-item array holding `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` for a reason and an empty array for null, and call it in `outputWarnings` with `getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason` read right after the scored call (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers` reports 0 failed.\n13:- [ ] T022 Add status cases with fixture databases: `commandVectorCoverage` with and without a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table, and `backend` for reachable, unreachable and model missing with `probeOllamaModel` mocked (`$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and at least five more passed than before.\n14:- [ ] T023 Add the sixth leg after the advisor leg: run `X adv