e manifest, its YAML stops at an approval before any `ollama pull`, `ollama serve` or `skill_graph_scan`, `--dry-run` stops after the plan and no step installs Ollama (`DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n20:- [ ] T029 Update the install contract test so it expects six steps with `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` as step 5 and `/doctor:setup` as step 6 (`DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n21:- [ ] T030 Add one entry for `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`: what it reads, that it writes and unloads nothing, its exit 2 and how to take a cold sample (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"measure-embedder-cost\" $ADV/scripts/README.md` prints at least one line.\n22:- [ ] T031 Build and rescan so the daemon serves the new code and the route's bridge has a vector. Run `npm --prefix $ADV run build`, then `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Verify: the scan exits 0 and `sqlite3 -readonly $ADV/database/skill-graph.sqlite 'select count(*) from vec_cmd_768'` prints the same number as `jq '[.entries[] | select(.embeddingText != null)] | length' $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`.\n23:- [ ] T032 Run `E` with the model loaded (`$S/cost-warm.json`). Verify: `node $E > $S/cost-warm.json` exits 0 and `jq -c '[.model.sizeBytes, .memory.serveRssKb, .memory.runnerRssKb, .warm.medianMs, .warm.p95Ms, .cli.medianMs]' $S/cost-warm.json` prints six numbers.\n24:- [ ] T033 Run `E` again after the model unloaded on its own (`$S/cost-cold.json`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, without unloading it by hand. Verify: `jq -c '[.cold.firstCallMs, .idle.serveRssKb]' $S/cost-cold.json` prints two numbers.\n25:- [ ] T034 Add row 5 `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` to the Step 2 table and renumber `/doctor:setup` to 6. Add a subsection \"Meaning Matching for Commands\" to section 2 with what a user gains, the cost table from T032 and T033 with the date (disk, idle memory, loaded memory, the 5 minute unload, warm and cold latency), the fact that the step asks before it pulls the model or starts the server and never installs Ollama, and the fact that a no keeps a phrase-only install. Add a troubleshooting row for `semantic_lane_off` (`INSTALL-SKILLED.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"meaning matching|skill-advisor embedder|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least three lines and each number in the table appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n26:- [ ] T035 Add one line to section 2 saying `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default behind a yes, and a subsection to section 12 with the same cost table, the setup route and the fact that `skill_graph_scan` writes the vectors and the database is gitignored (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder|vec_cmd\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints at least two lines.\n27:- [ ] T036 Add one sentence to section 12 saying `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes the hf-local server only and `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"includeEmbeddingsHealth\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints one line that names hf-local.\n35:- [ ] T037 Run the typecheck and the suite. Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `npm --prefix $ADV test` reports 0 failed.\n36:- [ ] T038 Rerun the default capture, the floor and the rollup. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n37:- [ ] T039 Rerun the real-embedding capture and the phrase-reach probe (`$S/real-embedding-after.json`). Verify: `node $C --real-embedding > $S/real-embedding-after.json` exits 0, `$M` over it prints tune combined 14 of 45, holdout combined 2 of 44, typed 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` exits 0.\n38:- [ ] T040 Run the doctor suites. Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed and `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n39:- [ ] T041 Run `$S/hook-latency.mjs` three times (`$S/hook-latency-after-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: the middle median is at most 25 ms over the T002 middle median and the middle p95 at most 40 ms over the T002 middle p95.\n40:- [ ] T042 Run the new setup leg's command once with the server running (`$S/setup-leg.txt`). Verify: `jq -c '.data.semanticLaneHealth | [.laneEnabled, .backend.state, .commandVectorCoverage.embedded > 0]'` over its output prints `[true,\"reachable\",true]`.\n41:- [ ] T043 Run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder --dry-run` in a session (`$S/route-dry-run.txt`). Verify: the transcript shows the plan with a cost and an undo per step and `STATUS=OK`, `git status --short` is unchanged and the database's `stat -f %m` is unchanged.\n42:- [ ] T044 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n88:- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n89:- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Phase 005 is merged: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line (T005).\n91:- [ ] CHK-004 [P1] `$S/cold-after-abort.txt` records whether a load continues after the client gives up (T003).\n\n[showing lines 52-189 of 189; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1d1f3bc54001J2zhLyotiucJIH.out]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"for f in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/00{5,6,7,8}-*