{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524066255,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f82ea1001099AjKFDwHC113","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f7d4b4001DYwi1um1ml0RYA","type":"tool","id":"call_ce981ecf946345d8ad367bd0","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/findings-registry.json"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/findings-registry.json","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/findings-registry.json"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"{\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"resolvedQuestions\\\":[],\\\"keyFindings\\\":[],\\\"ruledOutDirections\\\":[],\\\"metrics\\\":{\\\"iterationsCompleted\\\":0,\\\"openQuestions\\\":0,\\\"resolvedQuestions\\\":0,\\\"keyFindings\\\":0,\\\"convergenceScore\\\":0,\\\"coverageBySources\\\":{}}}\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/findings-registry.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524065441,"end":1794524066255}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524066259,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f7e088001ZoMJY9aCU62RnK","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1f7d4b4001DYwi1um1ml0RYA","type":"tool","id":"call_dbfba36eb7cf4e26955e4e8a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Research Strategy - ux lineage\n\n## 1. TOPIC\n\nFind further improvements to command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle: what the hook brief says and how a model reads it, when a command is offered, asked or started, the install and setup path for an external repository, and the performance and token cost the person pays for the brief. The cross-CLI question is the spine: whether a model on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin or dsh actually starts an offered command, and what stops it.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 2. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through the packet's `inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n- [ ] What does the hook brief actually put in front of a model today, and can a model on each of the six CLIs act on it without guessing the command id, its policy, the document to read and whether it was already offered?\n- [ ] Which before-arm runtime behaviour explains the start rates (claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12 or 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8), and what stops a model from starting an offered command?\n- [ ] Which command-discovery surface defects (the g5 `skill.md` collision and its siblings) keep a command from being offered or found on each runtime, and what detects them before a user hits one?\n- [ ] What does a person installing Skilled into an external repository see on first run, and where does the setup path still fail silently after the embedder work phase 008 plans?\n- [ ] What is the measured cost of the brief and of the hook (latency, tokens, cold start, embedder), and which part of that cost is invisible to the person paying it?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 3. NON-GOALS\n\n- Changing how skills are scored against each other, or re-deciding any operator answer recorded in `../../decision-record.md` (D1 to D5, Q001 to Q039).\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan. The lineage recommends only what comes after them or what they miss.\n- Editing or implementing anything. Findings and recommendations only; every recommendation names the file, the gain and the verification, and stops there.\n- Reading holdout prompt text. Corpus rows are read by the committed scripts only, never by this lineage.\n- Running pi, starting or stopping ollama, killing processes, running the full vitest suite, or any git write.\n\n---\n\n## 4. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Five iterations completed, or newInfoRatio below 0.05 after the three-iteration floor.\n- A source needed for a measurement cannot be read under the hard rules; the gap is recorded rather than guessed.\n- Any write would land outside `research/lineages/ux`.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 5. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 6. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 8. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 9. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 9A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 10A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\nWhat the hook brief actually emits, measured from the real hook: the head line, the directive block, the bytes and tokens per prompt, and whether the model-visible text carries enough to start the command without a guess.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 11. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nBounded pointer snapshot from the parent packet and its children. Read-only.\n\n- **Parent packet**: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/`. Phases 001 to 004 are Complete; 005 to 008 are Planned, not built. `spec.md`, `decision-record.md` (Q001 to Q039) and `goal.md` bind this lineage.\n- **005-recommendation-contract-and-brief**: one generated `COMMAND_ROWS` table in `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`; `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` in the public recommendation; the brief head becomes `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`; degraded path shows a command only when the prompt typed it; six golden heads.\n- **006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers**: one Gate 2 bullet in `AGENTS.md` (`COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`, read the document in full, `start` runs without `:auto`, `ask` asks once), a generated Cursor pointer block, a Gate 3 notice naming `/speckit:plan`, and `(parent-named only)` in a child brief.\n- **007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof**: transcript scorer and one-turn runner already built; before arm in flight. `scratch/runs-pre.jsonl` scored 2026-11-12: claude start 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8; `COMMAND:` line 0 of 24 on every runtime except dsh 1 of 8; pi unsafe 3.\n- **008-embedder-setup-and-cost**: `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, a `commandVectorCoverage` and `backend` status field, a 750 ms prompt-embedding deadline, a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` JSON warning, one `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` route behind a yes, a sixth `/doctor:setup` leg, and install-guide cost tables. The hook brief stays unchanged by operator decision Q037.\n- **g5**: `scratch/g5/result.txt` records that a command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill named after the folder, hiding every sibling command. `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists as a symlink to `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`; 13 siblings share that folder.\n- **Measured cost, 2026-11-12**: warm embed median 6.57 ms, p95 10.99 ms; advisor CLI 62.7 to 71.3 ms end to end; hook latency median about 200 ms, p95 about 260 ms over 44 probes; `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` 5,000; Claude hook budget 2,500 ms; CLI fallback budget 250 ms; brief token cap 80 (120 when ambiguous).\n- **Write surface**: this lineage only, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- **Source pointers**: `ADV/lib/render.ts` (brief head, directive block, caps), `ADV/lib/metrics.ts` (closed diagnostic schema), `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`.\n- **Reuse candidates**: `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, `005/scratch/brief-heads.mjs`, `007/scratch/hook-first-line.sh`.\n- **Integration points**: the model-visible brief, the closed-schema diagnostics record, the runtime mirror generators, the `/doctor:setup` legs, the install guide.\n- **Constraints**: no holdout text; read-only git; no pi; no ollama control; no process kills; no full vitest; writes only inside this lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 12. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls (self-capped at 12), 12 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 2, 5, 6-10A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` (this lineage)\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-12T22:54:00Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Research Strategy - ux lineage\\n\\n## 1. TOPIC\\n\\nFind further improvements to command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle: what the hook brief says and how a model reads it, when a command is offered, asked or started, the install and setup path for an external repository, and the performance and token cost the person pays for the brief. The cross-CLI question is the spine: whether a model on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin or dsh actually starts an offered command, and what stops it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 2. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through the packet's `inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\\n\\n- [ ] What does the hook brief actually put in front of a model today, and can a model on each of the six CLIs act on it without guessing the command id, its policy, the document to read and whether it was already offered?\\n- [ ] Which before-arm runtime behaviour explains the start rates (claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12 or 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8), and what stops a model from starting an offered command?\\n- [ ] Which command-discovery surface defects (the g5 `skill.md` collision and its siblings) keep a command from being offered or found on each runtime, and what detects them before a user hits one?\\n- [ ] What does a person installing Skilled into an external repository see on first run, and where does the setup path still fail silently after the embedder work phase 008 plans?\\n- [ ] What is the measured cost of the brief and of the hook (latency, tokens, cold start, embedder), and which part of that cost is invisible to the person paying it?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Changing how skills are scored against each other, or re-deciding any operator answer recorded in `../../decision-record.md` (D1 to D5, Q001 to Q039).\\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan. The lineage recommends only what comes after them or what they miss.\\n- Editing or implementing anything. Findings and recommendations only; every recommendation names the file, the gain and the verification, and stops there.\\n- Reading holdout prompt text. Corpus rows are read by the committed scripts only, never by this lineage.\\n- Running pi, starting or stopping ollama, killing processes, running the full vitest suite, or any git write.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Five iterations completed, or newInfoRatio below 0.05 after the three-iteration floor.\\n- A source needed for a measurement cannot be read under the hard rules; the gap is recorded rather than guessed.\\n- Any write would land outside `research/lineages/ux`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 5. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 8. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 9. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 9A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 10A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\\nWhat the hook brief actually emits, measured from the real hook: the head line, the directive block, the bytes and tokens per prompt, and whether the model-visible text carries enough to start the command without a guess.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 11. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nBounded pointer snapshot from the parent packet and its children. Read-only.\\n\\n- **Parent packet**: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/`. Phases 001 to 004 are Complete; 005 to 008 are Planned, not built. `spec.md`, `decision-record.md` (Q001 to Q039) and `goal.md` bind this lineage.\\n- **005-recommendation-contract-and-brief**: one generated `COMMAND_ROWS` table in `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`; `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId` in the public recommendation; the brief head becomes `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`; degraded path shows a command only when the prompt typed it; six golden heads.\\n- **006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers**: one Gate 2 bullet in `AGENTS.md` (`COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`, read the document in full, `start` runs without `:auto`, `ask` asks once), a generated Cursor pointer block, a Gate 3 notice naming `/speckit:plan`, and `(parent-named only)` in a child brief.\\n- **007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof**: transcript scorer and one-turn runner already built; before arm in flight. `scratch/runs-pre.jsonl` scored 2026-11-12: claude start 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8; `COMMAND:` line 0 of 24 on every runtime except dsh 1 of 8; pi unsafe 3.\\n- **008-embedder-setup-and-cost**: `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, a `commandVectorCoverage` and `backend` status field, a 750 ms prompt-embedding deadline, a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` JSON warning, one `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` route behind a yes, a sixth `/doctor:setup` leg, and install-guide cost tables. The hook brief stays unchanged by operator decision Q037.\\n- **g5**: `scratch/g5/result.txt` records that a command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill named after the folder, hiding every sibling command. `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists as a symlink to `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`; 13 siblings share that folder.\\n- **Measured cost, 2026-11-12**: warm embed median 6.57 ms, p95 10.99 ms; advisor CLI 62.7 to 71.3 ms end to end; hook latency median about 200 ms, p95 about 260 ms over 44 probes; `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` 5,000; Claude hook budget 2,500 ms; CLI fallback budget 250 ms; brief token cap 80 (120 when ambiguous).\\n- **Write surface**: this lineage only, `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- **Source pointers**: `ADV/lib/render.ts` (brief head, directive block, caps), `ADV/lib/metrics.ts` (closed diagnostic schema), `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`.\\n- **Reuse candidates**: `ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, `005/scratch/brief-heads.mjs`, `007/scratch/hook-first-line.sh`.\\n- **Integration points**: the model-visible brief, the closed-schema diagnostics record, the runtime mirror generators, the `/doctor:setup` legs, the install guide.\\n- **Constraints**: no holdout text; read-only git; no pi; no ollama control; no process kills; no full vitest; writes only inside this lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls (self-capped at 12), 12 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 2, 5, 6-10A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` (this lineage)\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-12T22:54:00Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-perf