{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524339230,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fc2e51001w6Zm0efT6sCBU3","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1fc20da001un3T0k6cHGbhxV","type":"tool","id":"call_fda82dcb841b49e6a499b06c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness after phases 005 to 008 — ux lineage\n\nDetached research lineage `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`. Topic: what to improve in command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle, with the cross-CLI start question as the spine. Every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain and the check that proves it. Phases 005 to 008 are planned, not built; nothing here repeats them.\n\n## 1. Executive verdict\n\n[Progressive — populated as iterations complete.]\n\n## 2. Answers to key questions\n\n- KQ1 What the brief emits and whether a model can act on it: **partly answered**. The brief is a 3-line, 240-296 character payload with a 320-character head budget, no document path and no offer state; the harness cannot distinguish an offer from a decline. See §3, findings 1-5.\n- KQ2 Which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates: open.\n- KQ3 Which discovery defects exist and what detects them: open.\n- KQ4 What an external repository sees on first run: open.\n- KQ5 What the brief and the hook cost: open.\n\n## 3. Findings by iteration\n\n### Iteration 1 — the model-visible brief\n\n1. The brief is 240-296 characters (about 60-74 tokens); 79 to 90 percent of a short brief is the same static directive block. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:162]\n2. The head uses 72 to 96 of its 320 available characters, leaving about 225 unused on every prompt. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:97]\n3. The brief names a command but never its document path; the 13 `create:*` commands have no Skill-tool route while `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n4. The closed diagnostic schema records `skillLabel` and `emittedBytes` but no offered command or policy, so an offer cannot be distinguished from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n\n## 4. Recommendations\n\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis. Iteration 1 candidates are in `iterations/iteration-001.md` under Recommendations.]\n\n## 5. Per-runtime notes\n\n[Progressive — iteration 2 onward.]\n\n## 6. Cost ledger\n\n| Item | Measured | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Brief payload, matching prompt | 258-296 chars, ~65-74 tokens | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\n| Brief payload, skipped prompt | 240 chars, ~60 tokens | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\n| Static directive block | 233 chars, ~58 tokens | `render.ts:162` |\n| Head budget | 320 chars (80 tokens) | `render.ts:97` |\n| Longest measured head | 96 chars | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\n\n## 7. Hard blockers and decisions\n\n- Operator answer Q025 leaves the `create` command ids as a recorded limitation, so renaming `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` is out of scope. Reaching the hidden commands needs the document path or a discovery check instead.\n- Operator answer Q037 keeps the hook brief unchanged for a degraded meaning lane, so no brief line may announce `semantic_lane_off`.\n\n## Eliminated Alternatives\n\n- Trimming the comment-hygiene directive block to reduce tokens: it carries a repo hard block and is deliberately injected beside every brief.\n- Renaming `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`: blocked by Q025; the document path and a discovery check reach the same commands.\n- Looking for an existing per-offer ledger: none exists; `AdvisorHookOutcomeRecord` has no command field.\n\n## Divergence Map\n\nNo divergent pivots. Saturated directions: none yet.\n\n## 12. Open Questions\n\n1. Does the offer-side signal change any start rate once recorded? Needs the post arm.\n2. Which runtimes have no command invocation surface at all, and does a document path close the gap?\n3. What does a cold-daemon first prompt cost? Cannot be measured without stopping the daemon under this lineage's rules.\n4. Does a policy word on a command reach the same workflow when the model takes the skill path? Iteration 2.\n\n## 13. Review cross-check\n\n[Progressive — checked at synthesis.]\n\n## 14. References\n\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis.]\n\n## 15. Implementation notes (non-goals of this run)\n\nNo implementation. Findings and recommendations only; every recommendation stops at the file, the gain and the check.\n\n## 16. Lineage metadata\n\n- Lineage: `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`, generation 1\n- Iterations complete: 1\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 on newInfoRatio, floor of 3 iterations\n- Write surface: this lineage directory only\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness after phases 005 to 008 — ux lineage\\n\\nDetached research lineage `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`. Topic: what to improve in command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle, with the cross-CLI start question as the spine. Every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain and the check that proves it. Phases 005 to 008 are planned, not built; nothing here repeats them.\\n\\n## 1. Executive verdict\\n\\n[Progressive — populated as iterations complete.]\\n\\n## 2. Answers to key questions\\n\\n- KQ1 What the brief emits and whether a model can act on it: **partly answered**. The brief is a 3-line, 240-296 character payload with a 320-character head budget, no document path and no offer state; the harness cannot distinguish an offer from a decline. See §3, findings 1-5.\\n- KQ2 Which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates: open.\\n- KQ3 Which discovery defects exist and what detects them: open.\\n- KQ4 What an external repository sees on first run: open.\\n- KQ5 What the brief and the hook cost: open.\\n\\n## 3. Findings by iteration\\n\\n### Iteration 1 — the model-visible brief\\n\\n1. The brief is 240-296 characters (about 60-74 tokens); 79 to 90 percent of a short brief is the same static directive block. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:162]\\n2. The head uses 72 to 96 of its 320 available characters, leaving about 225 unused on every prompt. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:97]\\n3. The brief names a command but never its document path; the 13 `create:*` commands have no Skill-tool route while `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\\n4. The closed diagnostic schema records `skillLabel` and `emittedBytes` but no offered command or policy, so an offer cannot be distinguished from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\\n5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\\n\\n## 4. Recommendations\\n\\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis. Iteration 1 candidates are in `iterations/iteration-001.md` under Recommendations.]\\n\\n## 5. Per-runtime notes\\n\\n[Progressive — iteration 2 onward.]\\n\\n## 6. Cost ledger\\n\\n| Item | Measured | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Brief payload, matching prompt | 258-296 chars, ~65-74 tokens | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\\n| Brief payload, skipped prompt | 240 chars, ~60 tokens | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\\n| Static directive block | 233 chars, ~58 tokens | `render.ts:162` |\\n| Head budget | 320 chars (80 tokens) | `render.ts:97` |\\n| Longest measured head | 96 chars | Hook probe, iteration 1 |\\n\\n## 7. Hard blockers and decisions\\n\\n- Operator answer Q025 leaves the `create` command ids as a recorded limitation, so renaming `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` is out of scope. Reaching the hidden commands needs the document path or a discovery check instead.\\n- Operator answer Q037 keeps the hook brief unchanged for a degraded meaning lane, so no brief line may announce `semantic_lane_off`.\\n\\n## Eliminated Alternatives\\n\\n- Trimming the comment-hygiene directive block to reduce tokens: it carries a repo hard block and is deliberately injected beside every brief.\\n- Renaming `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`: blocked by Q025; the document path and a discovery check reach the same commands.\\n- Looking for an existing per-offer ledger: none exists; `AdvisorHookOutcomeRecord` has no command field.\\n\\n## Divergence Map\\n\\nNo divergent pivots. Saturated directions: none yet.\\n\\n## 12. Open Questions\\n\\n1. Does the offer-side signal change any start rate once recorded? Needs the post arm.\\n2. Which runtimes have no command invocation surface at all, and does a document path close the gap?\\n3. What does a cold-daemon first prompt cost? Cannot be measured without stopping the daemon under this lineage's rules.\\n4. Does a policy word on a command reach the same workflow when the model takes the skill path? Iteration 2.\\n\\n## 13. Review cross-check\\n\\n[Progressive — checked at synthesis.]\\n\\n## 14. References\\n\\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis.]\\n\\n## 15. Implementation notes (non-goals of this run)\\n\\nNo implementation. Findings and recommendations only; every recommendation stops at the file, the gain and the check.\\n\\n## 16. Lineage metadata\\n\\n- Lineage: `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`, generation 1\\n- Iterations complete: 1\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 on newInfoRatio, floor of 3 iterations\\n- Write surface: this lineage directory only\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524327505,"end":1794524339230}}}}
