{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524375533,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fce887001059JD4Ecl070qw","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1fce21c00178mRHLXO3zybGk","type":"tool","id":"call_1f6feaa321a84d7187f4e81d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":22,"offset":60,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"output":"Read file AGENTS.md, lines 60-81\n60: | **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n61: | **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n62: \n63: #### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n64: 1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n65: 2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n66: 3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n67: - Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n68: - **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n69: - Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n70: - Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n71: \n72: #### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n73: **Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n74: \n75: - **Machine contract:** `system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts` (`classifyPrompt()`) owns the exact vocabulary; the sentence above paraphrases it.\n76: - **Options (stable labels, recommend one), asked via the `communication-handoff.md` §5 tool:**\n77:   - **A) Existing** - Continue in the detected/current spec or its current phase child when the work fits that scope. **Reply with the folder path.**\n78:   - **B) New** - Create a new top-level packet only when no existing packet suits the work. Decide independently whether it is standard or phased. **Reply with a new folder path.**\n79:   - **C) Related** - Use another existing packet, a child of an existing phase parent, a related standard packet split into phases once it meets both thresholds independently, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing same-track packet. **Reply with the folder or child path.**\n80:   - **D) Skip** - Explicitly skip documentation after the required warning or when an existing exemption applies. Never the default.\n81: - **Which to choose:** `system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md` §8 and §9 for the priority, `system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md` §2 for the two phase thresholds and the series parent.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 82]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file AGENTS.md, lines 60-81\n60: | **<40%** | Ask f