read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n74: \n75: - **Machine contract:** `system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts` (`classifyPrompt()`) owns the exact vocabulary; the sentence above paraphrases it.\n76: - **Options (stable labels, recommend one), asked via the `communication-handoff.md` §5 tool:**\n77:   - **A) Existing** - Continue in the detected/current spec or its current phase child when the work fits that scope. **Reply with the folder path.**\n78:   - **B) New** - Create a new top-level packet only when no existing packet suits the work. Decide independently whether it is standard or phased. **Reply with a new folder path.**\n79:   - **C) Related** - Use another existing packet, a child of an existing phase parent, a related standard packet split into phases once it meets both thresholds independently, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing same-track packet. **Reply with the folder or child path.**\n80:   - **D) Skip** - Explicitly skip documentation after the required warning or when an existing exemption applies. Never the default.\n81: - **Which to choose:** `system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md` §8 and §9 for the priority, `system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md` §2 for the two phase thresholds and the series parent.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 82]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":22,\"offset\":60,\"path\":\"AGENTS.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524375175,"end":1794524375533}}}}
