{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524579531,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1ff959d002T8jtpiKsUhoBap","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d1ff536c001WBi474TVCVdbe2","type":"tool","id":"call_b3580d56df72457a81a4963d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: What the before-arm transcripts say about starting a command\n\n## Focus\n\nWhy the before-arm start rates differ per runtime, what the model actually did on the rows it started and did not start, and whether the run-or-ask policy reaches the skill path as well as the command path. Chosen over the reducer's follow-up line because the reducer proposed continuing on the argued-route scorer defect, which is a P2 measurement detail already recorded with its fix; the first unchecked key question after KQ1 is the runtime-behaviour question, and the before arm is the only direct evidence for it.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Scored the before arm at 2026-11-12T23:01:49Z with the committed scorer: claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 3 of 12, opencode 5 of 12, dsh 4 of 12; `COMMAND:` line 0 everywhere except dsh 1 of 12.\n2. Re-scored every loadable before-arm session per row and split each runtime's rate by the row's derived policy, using the committed `loadSession`, `normalize` and `startState`.\n3. Joined the run log to the tune split of the command corpus on row id only, projecting `expected_command`, `expected_policy` and `row_type`; no prompt text was read.\n4. Read the changed paths of every run that wrote, to see what the model did instead of reading the command document.\n5. Read `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 and the derived-policy ladder in the bridge deriver.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The aggregate start rate hides a policy split that inverts per runtime.** Claude's 3 of 12 is **3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows**; opencode's 5 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 2 of 4 `run`; dsh's 4 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. The same number therefore describes opposite behaviour: claude adopts only checks it cannot improvise, while opencode and dsh adopt creation workflows. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640]\n\n2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587]\n\n3. **The run-or-ask policy does not reach the skill path.** Gate 2 today carries no command clause at all, and phase 006's bullet binds the policy words to a command that is in the brief. On an `ask` row with no command in the brief, devin's `/deep:ai-council` run created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi's `/deep:research` run wrote a retrieval fixture, both without asking and without the command's setup. The workflow a command owns is reachable through its skill, and that path carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/bullet-draft.txt:1]\n\n4. **No start in the before arm is attributable to the advisor.** The before brief never names a command, and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on claude, codex, pi and opencode and 1 of 12 on dsh, so every observed start came from the prompt's own affinity with a command document. A post-arm jump will not separate \"the offer worked\" from \"the same affinity\", unless the arm records what was offered per row. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557]\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Report the start rate per policy class.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, extend `--summary` to print `started` and `total` per `expected_policy` beside the aggregate. Gain: the claude 0 of 8 versus opencode 3 of 8 difference on mutating commands becomes visible, and a regression on the risky class cannot hide behind a rising aggregate. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.claude.pre.byPolicy'` prints `{\"run\":{\"started\":3,\"total\":4},\"start\":{\"started\":0,\"total\":8},\"ask\":{\"started\":0,\"total\":4}}`.\n2. **Add a write-target signal so a run that does the work by another path is not read as inert.** The same scorer reads each row's command metadata write target and reports `writeTargetHit` when a changed path falls under it. Gain: devin's five `/create:*` rows move from \"not started, no signal\" to \"not started, deliverable produced\", which is what the parent goal's outcome question needs; it also stops a future phase from \"fixing\" adoption that is already happening. Verify: the two devin `/create:agent` rows report `writeTargetHit: true`, and a synthetic case with an unrelated write reports `false`.\n3. **Bind the policy to the workflow, not only to the command.** Add one sentence to the Phase 006 bullet in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2: when a skill runs the workflow a command owns, that command's policy applies to the skill path too, so an `ask` command's workflow asks before its first write and a must-not-start command is not started from the skill either. Gain: closes the class the before arm already shows — devin's council scratch folder and pi's fixture write on `ask` rows — and makes the policy meaningful on the five runtimes that have no command invocation surface. Verify: `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, `agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`, and the post arm prints `unsafe 0` per runtime.\n4. **Record the offer per arm row and report starts per offer.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, call `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` for the row before the turn and record `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` on the run line; in the scorer, print `startsPerOffer` beside `startRate`. Gain: the only attribution the parent goal needs; a 24-run arm costs about 1.6 seconds of extra CLI time at the measured 65 ms per call. Verify: each run line carries both fields, and `--summary` prints `offered 12 of 12` and a starts-per-offer figure per runtime.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Treating the low claude start rate as a briefing failure.** The per-row split shows claude starts every read-only doctor row it meets (3 of 4) and no mutating one; a wording change would have to explain why the same brief works for one class and not the other, so the cause is the model's judgment about its own capability, not the text alone.\n- **Re-running the before arm to stabilise the numbers.** The arm is still growing (devin 16, opencode 14, dsh 12 at 23:01) and phase 007 owns the 24-per-runtime freeze; a research pass must not start CLI runs.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a per-policy figure in the existing summary: `--summary` prints one aggregate per arm and no policy breakdown, so the split had to be recomputed per session in this iteration. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640]\n- Looking for a rule that binds a command's policy to its skill path: Gate 2 has no command clause today, and the phase 006 bullet draft binds only \"a brief or advisor result that names a command\". [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: the strategy's Next Focus after iteration 1 pointed at the argued-route scorer defect, which is a P2 detail with its fix already recorded. Read as a finding follow-up rather than a focus area, and deferred; the first unchecked key question after KQ1 was used instead.\n- Contradictory evidence: the before arm grew during the iteration (devin 12 to 16 runs, opencode 9 to 14, dsh 11 to 12), so the summary printed at 22:53 and the one printed at 23:01 disagree. Both are recorded with their timestamps; the per-row split was recomputed against the 23:01 log.\n- Missing dependencies: pi and devin sessions were not re-scored per row (pi needs its agent session log, devin a SQLite read), so their policy split is taken from the run log and the aggregate only. Their unsafe counts are the scorer's.\n- Partial success: 4 findings, all with a reproduced number or a cited path; the per-policy split covers four of six runtimes.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587,640`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (tune split, projected fields only)\n- `AGENTS.md:63`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/bullet-draft.txt:1`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:133`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/steer.md`\n- Per-row re-score of 50 before-arm sessions through `loadSession`, `normalize` and `startState`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.88\n- Questions addressed: KQ2 (which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates, and what stops a model)\n- Questions answered: KQ2 — the split is explained: adoption follows capability, not the aggregate rate, and the policy does not reach the skill path\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: re-scoring per row instead of trusting the aggregate turned a flat 3 of 12 into 3 of 4 read-only and 0 of 8 mutating, which is a different story and a different recommendation. Reading the changed paths showed devin producing the command's exact artifacts, which exposed the metric's path-versus-outcome confusion.\n- What did not work and why: joining on an aggregate first produced a \"claude starts 3 of 12\" claim that would have hidden the class inversion; the aggregate is only useful after the split exists.\n- What I would do differently: re-score pi and devin per row in the same pass, so all six runtimes have the same evidence quality.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nThe discovery surface per runtime: how many of the 44 tracked commands a model can actually find on each CLI, what the `skill.md` collision costs beyond Claude, and what static check would catch a collapsed command folder before a user does.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 2: What the before-arm transcripts say about starting a command\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nWhy the before-arm start rates differ per runtime, what the model actually did on the rows it started and did not start, and whether the run-or-ask policy reaches the skill path as well as the command path. Chosen over the reducer's follow-up line because the reducer proposed continuing on the argued-route scorer defect, which is a P2 measurement detail already recorded with its fix; the first unchecked key question after KQ1 is the runtime-behaviour question, and the before arm is the only direct evidence for it.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Scored the before arm at 2026-11-12T23:01:49Z with the committed scorer: claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 3 of 12, opencode 5 of 12, dsh 4 of 12; `COMMAND:` line 0 everywhere except dsh 1 of 12.\\n2. Re-scored every loadable before-arm session per row and split each runtime's rate by the row's derived policy, using the committed `loadSession`, `normalize` and `startState`.\\n3. Joined the run log to the tune split of the command corpus on row id only, projecting `expected_command`, `expected_policy` and `row_type`; no prompt text was read.\\n4. Read the changed paths of every run that wrote, to see what the model did instead of reading the command document.\\n5. Read `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 and the derived-policy ladder in the bridge deriver.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The aggregate start rate hides a policy split that inverts per runtime.** Claude's 3 of 12 is **3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows**; opencode's 5 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 2 of 4 `run`; dsh's 4 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. The same number therefore describes opposite behaviour: claude adopts only checks it cannot improvise, while opencode and dsh adopt creation workflows. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640]\\n\\n2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587]\\n\\n3. **The run-or-ask policy does not reach the skill path.** Gate 2 today carries no command clause at all, and phase 006's bullet binds the policy words to a command that is in the brief. On an `ask` row with no command in the brief, devin's `/deep:ai-council` run created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi's `/deep:research` run wrote a retrieval fixture, both without asking and without the command's setup. The workflow a command owns is reachable through its skill, and that path carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/bullet-draft.txt:1]\\n\\n4. **No start in the before arm is attributable to the advisor.** The before brief never names a command, and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on claude, codex, pi and opencode and 1 of 12 on dsh, so every observed start came from the prompt's own affinity with a command document. A post-arm jump will not separate \\\"the offer worked\\\" from \\\"the same affinity\\\", unless the arm records what was offered per row. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557]\\n\\n## Recommendations\\n\\n1. **Report the start rate per policy class.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, extend `--summary` to print `started` and `total` per `expected_policy` beside the aggregate. Gain: the claude 0 of 8 versus opencode 3 of 8 difference on mutating commands becomes visible, and a regression on the risky class cannot hide behind a rising aggregate. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.claude.pre.byPolicy'` prints `{\\\"run\\\":{\\\"started\\\":3,\\\"total\\\":4},\\\"start\\\":{\\\"started\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":8},\\\"ask\\\":{\\\"started\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":4}}`.\\n2. **Add a write-target signal so a run that does the work by another path is not read as inert.** The same scorer reads each row's command metadata write target and reports `writeTargetHit` when a changed path falls under it. Gain: devin's five `/create:*` rows move from \\\"not started, no signal\\\" to \\\"not started, deliverable produced\\\", which is what the parent goal's outcome question needs; it also stops a future phase from \\\"fixing\\\" adoption that is already happening. Verify: the two devin `/create:agent` rows report `writeTargetHit: true`, and a synthetic case with an unrelated write reports `false`.\\n3. **Bind the policy to the workflow, not only to the command.** Add one sentence to the Phase 006 bullet in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2: when a skill runs the workflow a command owns, that command's policy applies to the skill path too, so an `ask` command's workflow asks before its first write and a must-not-start command is not started from the skill either. Gain: closes the class the before arm already shows — devin's council scratch folder and pi's fixture write on `ask` rows — and makes the policy meaningful on the five runtimes that have no command invocation surface. Verify: `rg -c \\\"policy applies to the skill path\\\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, `agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`, and the post arm prints `unsafe 0` per runtime.\\n4. **Record the offer per arm row and report starts per offer.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, call `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` for the row before the turn and record `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` on the run line; in the scorer, print `startsPerOffer` beside `startRate`. Gain: the only attribution the parent goal needs; a 24-run arm costs about 1.6 seconds of extra CLI time at the measured 65 ms per call. Verify: each run line carries both fields, and `--summary` prints `offered 12 of 12` and a starts-per-offer figure per runtime.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Treating the low claude start rate as a briefing failure.** The per-row split shows claude starts every read-only doctor row it meets (3 of 4) and no mutating one; a wording change would have to explain why the same brief works for one class and not the other, so the cause is the model's judgment about its own capability, not the text alone.\\n- **Re-running the before arm to stabilise the numbers.** The arm is still growing (devin 16, opencode 14, dsh 12 at 23:01) and phase 007 owns the 24-per-runtime freeze; a research pass must not start CLI runs.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a per-policy figure in the existing summary: `--summary` prints one aggregate per arm and no policy breakdown, so the split had to be recomputed per session in this iteration. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640]\\n- Looking for a rule that binds a command's policy to its skill path: Gate 2 has no command clause today, and the phase 006 bullet draft binds only \\\"a brief or advisor result that names a command\\\". [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: the strategy's Next Focus after iteration 1 pointed at the argued-route scorer defect, which is a P2 detail with its fix already recorded. Read as a finding follow-up rather than a focus area, and deferred; the first unchecked key question after KQ1 was used instead.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the before arm grew during the iteration (devin 12 to 16 runs, opencode 9 to 14, dsh 11 to 12), so the summary printed at 22:53 and the one printed at 23:01 disagree. Both are recorded with their timestamps; the per-row split was recomputed against the 23:01 log.\\n- Missing dependencies: pi and devin sessions were not re-scored per row (pi needs its agent session log, devin a SQLite read), so their policy split is taken from the run log and the aggregate only. Their unsafe counts are the scorer's.\\n- Partial success: 4 findings, all with a reproduced number or a cited path; the per-policy split covers four of six runtimes.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587,640`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` (tune split, projected fields only)\\n- `AGENTS.md:63`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/bullet-draft.txt:1`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:133`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/steer.md`\\n- Per-row re-score of 50 before-arm sessions through `loadSession`, `normalize` and `startState`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.88\\n- Questions addressed: KQ2 (which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates, and what stops a model)\\n- Questions answered: KQ2 — the split is explained: adoption follows capability, not the aggregate rate, and the policy does not reach the skill path\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: re-scoring per row instead of trusting the aggregate turned a flat 3 of 12 into 3 of 4 read-only and 0 of 8 mutating, which is a different story and a different recommendation. Reading the changed paths showed devin producing the command's exact artifacts, which exposed the metric's path-versus-outcome confusion.\\n- What did not work and why: joining on an aggregate first produced a \\\"claude starts 3 of 12\\\" claim that would have hidden the class inversion; the aggregate is only useful after the split exists.\\n- What I would do differently: re-score pi and devin per row in the same pass, so all six runtimes have the same evidence quality.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nThe discovery surface per runtime: how many of the 44 tracked commands a model can actually find on each CLI, what the `skill.md` collision costs beyond Claude, and what static check would catch a collapsed command folder before a user does.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524550557,"end":1794524579531}}}}
