{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524613135,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d200799a001O2mLEqWfr36U2X","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d200561e001zQiqp0fwkbGEBS","type":"tool","id":"call_908adc9ecccc4c2abbf40fd7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md","oldString":"2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587]","newString":"2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`: 5 of devin's 8 mutating rows wrote, while 0 of 8 scored started. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number, and the declared \"write target per command\" from phase 002 is prose in `gate3_location` (\"a new or updated OpenCode skill package at --path\"), not a path prefix any check can match. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json]"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n@@ -15,9 +15,9 @@\n ## Findings\n \n 1. **The aggregate start rate hides a policy split that inverts per runtime.** Claude's 3 of 12 is **3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows**; opencode's 5 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 2 of 4 `run`; dsh's 4 of 12 is 3 of 8 `start` and 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. The same number therefore describes opposite behaviour: claude adopts only checks it cannot improvise, while opencode and dsh adopt creation workflows. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:640]\n \n-2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587]\n+2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`: 5 of devin's 8 mutating rows wrote, while 0 of 8 scored started. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number, and the declared \"write target per command\" from phase 002 is prose in `gate3_location` (\"a new or updated OpenCode skill package at --path\"), not a path prefix any check can match. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json]\n \n 3. **The run-or-ask policy does not reach the skill path.** Gate 2 today carries no command clause at all, and phase 006's bullet binds the policy words to a command that is in the brief. On an `ask` row with no command in the brief, devin's `/deep:ai-council` run created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi's `/deep:research` run wrote a retrieval fixture, both without asking and without the command's setup. The workflow a command owns is reachable through its skill, and that path carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/bullet-draft.txt:1]\n \n 4. **No start in the before arm is attributable to the advisor.** The before brief never names a command, and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on claude, codex, pi and opencode and 1 of 12 on dsh, so every observed start came from the prompt's own affinity with a command document. A post-arm jump will not separate \"the offer worked\" from \"the same affinity\", unless the arm records what was offered per row. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557]\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\",\"oldString\":\"2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587]\",\"newString\":\"2. **The start rate measures the path, not the outcome.** Devin's two `/create:agent` runs wrote `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` — the exact artifacts the command exists to produce — yet score `started: false` because they never read the document. The same holds for `/create:command` writing `.skilled/skills/prompt-shortcut/`: 5 of devin's 8 mutating rows wrote, while 0 of 8 scored started. A run that does the work its own way and a run that does nothing are indistinguishable in the headline number, and the declared \\\"write target per command\\\" from phase 002 is prose in `gate3_location` (\\\"a new or updated OpenCode skill package at --path\\\"), not a path prefix any check can match. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:587] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json]\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524608922,"end":1794524613135}}}}
