{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524623795,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d200a07d001D4n6xWnDB3cWvx","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d20092d4001GIaKX1JGbRtaZi","type":"tool","id":"call_60df4fb49e0849fdabce0c77","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"2. **Report a `wrote` count beside `started`, per policy class.** In the same `--summary` output, count runs with at least one changed path. Gain: devin's 0 of 8 mutating starts become 0 started and 5 of 8 wrote, so a run that did the work by another path is no longer read as inert; codex stays 0 and 0, which is the real contrast. This uses the run log's existing `changedPaths`, so no new metadata is needed. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.devin.pre.byPolicy.start'` prints `{\"started\":0,\"total\":8,\"wrote\":5}`.\n3. **Give the declared write target a machine-readable form before any check depends on it.** Phase 002 ships `gate3_location` as prose, so no automated match exists; when a later phase needs one, add `write_targets: [\"<path prefix>\", ...]` to each `command-metadata.json` entry that produces a file, and carry it through `derive-command-bridges.cjs` into the generated inventory. Gain: the outcome question becomes answerable per command instead of per run. Verify: `jq -r '.[] | select(.command==\"/create:agent\") | .write_targets' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json` prints the three agent roots and `node $D --check` prints `fresh`.","oldString":"2. **Add a write-target signal so a run that does the work by another path is not read as inert.** The same scorer reads each row's command metadata write target and reports `writeTargetHit` when a changed path falls under it. Gain: devin's five `/create:*` rows move from \"not started, no signal\" to \"not started, deliverable produced\", which is what the parent goal's outcome question needs; it also stops a future phase from \"fixing\" adoption that is already happening. Verify: the two devin `/create:agent` rows report `writeTargetHit: true`, and a synthetic case with an unrelated write reports `false`.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\n@@ -24,9 +24,10 @@\n \n ## Recommendations\n \n 1. **Report the start rate per policy class.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, extend `--summary` to print `started` and `total` per `expected_policy` beside the aggregate. Gain: the claude 0 of 8 versus opencode 3 of 8 difference on mutating commands becomes visible, and a regression on the risky class cannot hide behind a rising aggregate. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.claude.pre.byPolicy'` prints `{\"run\":{\"started\":3,\"total\":4},\"start\":{\"started\":0,\"total\":8},\"ask\":{\"started\":0,\"total\":4}}`.\n-2. **Add a write-target signal so a run that does the work by another path is not read as inert.** The same scorer reads each row's command metadata write target and reports `writeTargetHit` when a changed path falls under it. Gain: devin's five `/create:*` rows move from \"not started, no signal\" to \"not started, deliverable produced\", which is what the parent goal's outcome question needs; it also stops a future phase from \"fixing\" adoption that is already happening. Verify: the two devin `/create:agent` rows report `writeTargetHit: true`, and a synthetic case with an unrelated write reports `false`.\n+2. **Report a `wrote` count beside `started`, per policy class.** In the same `--summary` output, count runs with at least one changed path. Gain: devin's 0 of 8 mutating starts become 0 started and 5 of 8 wrote, so a run that did the work by another path is no longer read as inert; codex stays 0 and 0, which is the real contrast. This uses the run log's existing `changedPaths`, so no new metadata is needed. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.devin.pre.byPolicy.start'` prints `{\"started\":0,\"total\":8,\"wrote\":5}`.\n+3. **Give the declared write target a machine-readable form before any check depends on it.** Phase 002 ships `gate3_location` as prose, so no automated match exists; when a later phase needs one, add `write_targets: [\"<path prefix>\", ...]` to each `command-metadata.json` entry that produces a file, and carry it through `derive-command-bridges.cjs` into the generated inventory. Gain: the outcome question becomes answerable per command instead of per run. Verify: `jq -r '.[] | select(.command==\"/create:agent\") | .write_targets' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json` prints the three agent roots and `node $D --check` prints `fresh`.\n 3. **Bind the policy to the workflow, not only to the command.** Add one sentence to the Phase 006 bullet in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2: when a skill runs the workflow a command owns, that command's policy applies to the skill path too, so an `ask` command's workflow asks before its first write and a must-not-start command is not started from the skill either. Gain: closes the class the before arm already shows — devin's council scratch folder and pi's fixture write on `ask` rows — and makes the policy meaningful on the five runtimes that have no command invocation surface. Verify: `rg -c \"policy applies to the skill path\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, `agents-md-check.cjs --json | jq -r .status` prints `OK`, and the post arm prints `unsafe 0` per runtime.\n 4. **Record the offer per arm row and report starts per offer.** In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, call `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` for the row before the turn and record `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` on the run line; in the scorer, print `startsPerOffer` beside `startRate`. Gain: the only attribution the parent goal needs; a 24-run arm costs about 1.6 seconds of extra CLI time at the measured 65 ms per call. Verify: each run line carries both fields, and `--summary` prints `offered 12 of 12` and a starts-per-offer figure per runtime.\n \n ## Ruled Out\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"2. **Report a `wrote` count beside `started`, per policy class.** In the same `--summary` output, count runs with at least one changed path. Gain: devin's 0 of 8 mutating starts become 0 started and 5 of 8 wrote, so a run that did the work by another path is no longer read as inert; codex stays 0 and 0, which is the real contrast. This uses the run log's existing `changedPaths`, so no new metadata is needed. Verify: `node $S --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --json | jq '.devin.pre.byPolicy.start'` prints `{\\\"started\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":8,\\\"wrote\\\":5}`.\\n3. **Give the declared write target a machine-readable form before any check depends on it.** Phase 002 ships `gate3_location` as prose, so no automated match exists; when a later phase needs one, add `write_targets: [\\\"<path prefix>\\\", ...]` to each `command-metadata.json` entry that produces a file, and carry it through `derive-command-bridges.cjs` into the generated inventory. Gain: the outcome question becomes answerable per command instead of per run. Verify: `jq -r '.[] | select(.command==\\\"/create:agent\\\") | .write_targets' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json` prints the three agent roots and `node $D --check` prints `fresh`.\",\"oldString\":\"2. **Add a write-target signal so a run that does the work by another path is not read as inert.** The same scorer reads each row's command metadata write target and reports `writeTargetHit` when a changed path falls under it. Gain: devin's five `/create:*` rows move from \\\"not started, no signal\\\" to \\\"not started, deliverable produced\\\", which is what the parent goal's outcome question needs; it also stops a future phase from \\\"fixing\\\" adoption that is already happening. Verify: the two devin `/create:agent` rows report `writeTargetHit: true`, and a synthetic case with an unrelated write reports `false`.\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524618877,"end":1794524623795}}}}
