`commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md\n@@ -23,8 +23,15 @@\n 3. The brief names a command but never its document path; the 13 `create:*` commands have no Skill-tool route while `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n 4. The closed diagnostic schema records `skillLabel` and `emittedBytes` but no offered command or policy, so an offer cannot be distinguished from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n 5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n \n+### Iteration 2 — before-arm behaviour and the policy gap\n+\n+6. The aggregate start rate inverts by policy class: claude is 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; opencode and dsh are 3 of 8 `start` and 2 or 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n+7. The start rate measures the path, not the outcome: devin produced `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` from `/create:agent` rows while scoring `started: false`; 5 of 8 mutating devin rows wrote. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n+8. The run-or-ask policy stops at the command: devin created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi wrote a retrieval fixture on `ask` rows without asking, because the skill path that runs the same workflow carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n+9. No before-arm start is attributable to the advisor; the brief names no command and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on four runtimes and 1 of 12 on dsh.\n+\n ## 4. Recommendations\n \n [Progressive — consolidated at synthesis. Iteration 1 candidates are in `iterations/iteration-001.md` under Recommendations.]\n \n","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\\n\\n### Iteration 2 — before-arm behaviour and the policy gap\\n\\n6. The aggregate start rate inverts by policy class: claude is 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; opencode and dsh are 3 of 8 `start` and 2 or 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\\n7. The start rate measures the path, not the outcome: devin produced `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` from `/create:agent` rows while scoring `started: false`; 5 of 8 mutating devin rows wrote. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\\n8. The run-or-ask policy stops at the command: devin created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi wrote a retrieval fixture on `ask` rows without asking, because the skill path that runs the same workflow carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\\n9. No before-arm start is attributable to the advisor; the brief names no command and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on four runtimes and 1 of 12 on dsh.\",\"oldString\":\"5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524700714,"end":1794524707664}}}}
