{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524921759,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d20539ec001zpsK58mQJA1hsd","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d2050e5b001jCmLZzSwsehWWw","type":"tool","id":"call_ff6f104d4b30436485030e83","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n -i \"cold start|cold-start|daemon start|starts the daemon|first prompt\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md INSTALL-SKILLED.md 2>/dev/null | head -12; echo ===; rg -n -i \"daemon\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/*.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/*.ts 2>/dev/null | rg -i \"start|spawn\" | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:105:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:72:That is the whole install. The CLI starts the daemon on first use, so there is nothing to register or start by hand.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:163:Prompt-time surfaces run the same scorer, which is why a shim smoke test doubles as a hook smoke test. There is no plugin bridge or MCP client in the chain: the hooks and the OpenCode plugin shell out to `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, and the CLI starts the daemon through `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` when the socket is cold.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:291:Phase `002/jina-swap-and-reindex` runbook plus phase `004/skill-graph-db-writer-cross-wire` together make the swap safe end-to-end. The writer dispatcher (`refreshSkillEmbeddings()`) routes through `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` when an active pointer is set and falls back to the legacy `createEmbeddingsProvider` factory only when the cascade has not yet resolved (e.g. cold start before any probe succeeds).\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:105:| `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:72:That is the whole install. The CLI starts the daemon on first use, so there is nothing to register or start by hand.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:163:Prompt-time surfaces run the same scorer, which is why a shim smoke test doubles as a hook smoke test. There is no plugin bridge or MCP client in the chain: the hooks and the OpenCode plugin shell out to `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, and the CLI starts the daemon through `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` when the socket is cold.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:291:Phase `002/jina-swap-and-reindex` runbook plus phase `004/skill-graph-db-writer-cross-wire` together make the swap safe end-to-end. The writer dispatcher (`refreshSkillEmbeddings()`) routes through `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` when an active pointer is set and falls back to the legacy `createEmbeddingsProvider` factory only when the cascade has not yet resolved (e.g. cold start before any probe succeeds).\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n -i \\\"cold start|cold-start|daemon start|starts the daemon|first prompt\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md INSTALL-SKILLED.md 2>/dev/null | head -12; echo ===; rg -n -i \\\"daemon\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/*.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/*.ts 2>/dev/null | rg -i \\\"start|spawn\\\" | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524920300,"end":1794524921759}}}}
