s/schema.ts:255: * Decide whether the persisted active-embedder pointer needs cascade\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:275: * Map a manifest's `BackendKind` to the cascade's `provider` taxonomy. The\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:276: * cascade distinguishes Voyage from OpenAI at the api tier, but\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:297: * shared registry no longer knows about, invoke the shared cascade\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:301: * The shared cascade probes (in order): Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:304: * cascade is text-tuned by design, but it is plumbed through for future\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:307:export async function ensureActiveEmbedder(\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:317:      // derivation, without re-running the cascade.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:334:      // Derive the cascade-tier provider from the manifest's backend kind so\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts:362:  // Persist the winner explicitly. The real cascade also persists via\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts:29:export type HealthRequest = (target: HealthTarget, timeoutMs: number) => Promise<unknown>;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts:182:function requestHealth(target: HealthTarget, timeoutMs: number): Promise<unknown> {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts:225:      outgoing.destroy(new HealthProbeError('timeout', `Health probe timed out after ${timeoutMs} ms`));\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts:226:    }, timeoutMs);\n.sk