{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524955458,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d205be93002igDs7MRcyMBq0v","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d2058471001IJd4ISD2K6Fy34","type":"tool","id":"call_76aa09f2e0744b1dbf128956","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"spell commands with a hyphen|your own files there stay untouched|Confirms the whole setup|Check the Install|It checks the install\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md; echo ===; rg -n \"ensureActiveEmbedder|first daemon start\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -4; echo ===; rg -n \"Add merge links\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs"},"output":"55:### Check the Install\n63:It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n65:Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n118:| 5 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n143:With `auto`, a folder your project already has stays a real folder. Each entry inside it becomes its own link, and your own files there stay untouched.\n===\n280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n344:4. Restart the daemon. `ensureActiveEmbedder()` either honours your override or runs the cascade. The first scan or watcher tick populates `vec_<active.dim>` via the adapter dispatcher.\n===\n821: * Add merge links under a real directory, preserving every local path.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"55:### Check the Install\n63:It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n65:Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n118:| 5 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n143:With `auto`, a folder your project already has stays a real folder. Each entry inside it becomes its own link, and your own files there stay untouched.\n===\n280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n344:4. Restart the daemon. `ensureActiveEmbedder()` either honours your override or runs the cascade. The first scan or watcher tick populates `vec_<active.dim>` via the adapter dispatcher.\n===\n821: * Add merge links under a real directory, preserving every local path.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"spell commands with a hyphen|your own files there stay untouched|Confirms the whole setup|Check the Install|It checks the install\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md; echo ===; rg -n \\\"ensureActiveEmbedder|first daemon start\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -4; echo ===; rg -n \\\"Add merge links\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524954259,"end":1794524955458}}}}
