{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794525293566,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","part":{"partID":"prt_1d20ae54e001RzoTnvHIkT7e7S","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4b2cffeAWQl6ZGxUDL6xW","messageID":"msg_1d20ad20d0019tV4xbW3TK0Ds5","type":"tool","id":"call_82db9510be9247dea1a1e392","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && d=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' $d/deep-research-strategy.md | grep -E '^- \\[' ; echo \"=== iterations in state:\"; jq -s '[.[]|select(.type==\"iteration\")]|length' $d/deep-research-state.jsonl; jq -s '[.[]|select(.type==\"event\")|.event // .stem]|group_by(.)|map({e:.[0],n:length})' $d/deep-research-state.jsonl | head -c 400"},"output":"- [ ] What does the hook brief actually put in front of a model today, and can a model on each of the six CLIs act on it without guessing the command id, its policy, the document to read and whether it was already offered?\n- [x] Which before-arm runtime behaviour explains the start rates (claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12 or 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8), and what stops a model from starting an offered command?\n- [ ] Which command-discovery surface defects (the g5 `skill.md` collision and its siblings) keep a command from being offered or found on each runtime, and what detects them before a user hits one?\n- [x] What does a person installing Skilled into an external repository see on first run, and where does the setup path still fail silently after the embedder work phase 008 plans?\n- [x] What is the measured cost of the brief and of the hook (latency, tokens, cold start, embedder), and which part of that cost is invisible to the person paying it?\n=== iterations in state:\n5\n[\n  {\n    \"e\": \"synthesis_complete\",\n    \"n\": 1\n  }\n]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] What does the hook brief actually put in front of a model today, and can a model on each of the six CLIs act on it without guessing the command id, its policy, the document to read and whether it was already offered?\n- [x] Which before-arm runtime behaviour explains the start rates (claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12 or 12, opencode 4 of 9, dsh 3 of 8), and what stops a model from starting an offered command?\n- [ ] Which command-discovery surface defects (the g5 `skill.md` collision and its siblings) keep a command from being offered or found on each runtime, and what detects them before a user hits one?\n- [x] What does a person installing Skilled into an external repository see on first run, and where does the setup path still fail silently after the embedder work phase 008 plans?\n- [x] What is the measured cost of the brief and of the hook (latency, tokens, cold start, embedder), and which part of that cost is invisible to the person paying it?\n=== iterations in state:\n5\n[\n  {\n    \"e\": \"synthesis_complete\",\n    \"n\": 1\n  }\n]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && d=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/ux && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' $d/deep-research-strategy.md | grep -E '^- \\\\[' ; echo \\\"=== iterations in state:\\\"; jq -s '[.[]|select(.type==\\\"iteration\\\")]|length' $d/deep-research-state.jsonl; jq -s '[.[]|select(.type==\\\"event\\\")|.event // .stem]|group_by(.)|map({e:.[0],n:length})' $d/deep-research-state.jsonl | head -c 400\"}"},"time":{"start":1794525291854,"end":1794525293566}}}}
